window.DOCS["6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771"]={"id":"6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771","summary":{"title_zh":"第一工作小組報告草案","what":"這份文件為第一工作小組報告草案，英文全文為大會第十七次會議、卡塔赫納生物安全議定書第十二次締約方會議及名古屋議定書第六次締約方會議之共同文件（CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1）。文件由工作小組主席 Gaute Hanssen（挪威）主持之第一工作小組提出，記錄三場會議期間各議程項目的討論進度與處理結果，並準備提交全會通過。","points":["同意成立聯絡小組（第8(a)項，資源動員），進一步討論決議草案，重點包括擴大捐助者基礎之選項、財務機制制度結構之附加標準、三項研究報告相關段落及秘書處提出之修正，以及草案中剩餘的括號文字。","同意成立聯絡小組（第8(b)項，財務機制），處理第六及第七次附屬執行機構會議之未決事項；並由主席另設主席之友小組，探討可能的共識領域。","同意成立聯絡小組（第9(a)項），處理昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要全球進度審查決議草案中的括號文字。","同意成立聯絡小組（第10(a)與10(b)(i)項），處理第8(j)條相關工作計畫及其指引之未解決問題。","數位序列資訊（DSI）與卡利基金：主席另設主席之友小組（閉門進行），審議卡利基金諒解備忘錄及其他營運文件，並得處理決議草案第29與30段有關指導委員會成員遴選之議題；同意成立聯絡小組，處理DSI決議草案第I至IX節。","同意成立聯絡小組（第14(a)項），處理生物多樣性主流化決議草案之文字；次國家級政府與城市參與（第14(b)項）則由吐瓦魯代表協調之小組進行非正式討論。","同意成立聯絡小組（第19項），處理會議效率相關三份決議草案中的全部括號文字。","第15項性別行動計畫決議草案已獲工作小組核可，作為 CBD/COP/17/L.2 提交全會；第20項多年度工作計畫決議草案，主席表示將與秘書處協商修訂。"],"open":["擴大捐助者基礎之選項、財務機制制度結構之附加標準，以及三項研究報告相關段落之修正，尚未定案。","昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要全球進度審查、第8(j)條相關、DSI與卡利基金制度安排（含諒解備忘錄內容），以及主流化與次國家級政府參與等決議草案，其括號文字與未達成共識部分仍未解決。","DSI決議草案第29與30段（指導委員會成員遴選）之處理方式尚未定案。","第10(b)(ii)項（第8(j)條工作計畫之術語表）延後審議，待主席修訂草案；第10(c)與10(d)項草案亦待修訂。","第12(a)項（能力建構與發展及技術與科學合作）與第13項（與其他公約下國際組織及機構之合作）之括號文字，仍在聯絡小組處理中。","報告多處仍標註為待完成（to be completed），尚未完成。"]},"summaryReviewed":true,"pages":[{"p":"p001","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p001.md","en":"                             CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n                                                                                      Distr.: Limited\n                                                                                      28 October 2026\n                                                                                      Original: English\n\n\n\n\nConference of the Parties to             Conference of the Parties to             Conference of the Parties to the\nthe Convention on Biological             the Convention on Biological             Convention on Biological\nDiversity                                Diversity serving as the                 Diversity serving as the meeting\nSeventeenth meeting                      meeting of the Parties to the            of the Parties to the Nagoya\nYerevan, 19–30 October 2026              Cartagena Protocol on                    Protocol on Access to Genetic\nAgenda item 22                           Biosafety                                Resources and the Fair and\nAdoption of the report                   Twelfth meeting                          Equitable Sharing of Benefits\n                                         Yerevan, 19–30 October 2026              Arising from Their Utilization\n                                         Agenda item 19                           Sixth meeting\n                                         Adoption of the report                   Yerevan, 19–30 October 2026\n                                                                                  Agenda item 17\n                                                                                  Adoption of the report\n\n       Draft report of Working Group I\n\nIntroduction\n       1.     Working Group I, chaired by Gaute Hanssen (Norway), met to consider items 8 to 15, 19\n       and 20 of the agenda for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention\n       on Biological Diversity (see sect. I), item 12 of the agenda for the twelfth meeting of the Conference\n       of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol on Biosafety (see sect. II)\n       and items 5 and 7 to 15 of the agenda for the sixth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving\n       as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair\n       and Equitable Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization (see sect. III).\n       2.     [to be completed]\n\nI.     Seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention\n       on Biological Diversity\nItem 8\nResource mobilization and financial mechanism\n\n(a)    Resource mobilization\n       3.     Working Group I began its consideration of agenda sub-item 8 (a) at its 1st session, on\n       19 October. It had before it a draft decision1 and a note by the Secretariat on resource mobilization\n       and the financial mechanism.2 Four information documents had also been issued in relation to sub-\n       item 8 (a): a study on the relationship between biodiversity and climate finance, 3 a study on the\n       relationship between debt sustainability and implementation of the Convention,4 a study on how the\n\n1 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 8 (a).\n2 CBD/COP/17/5.\n3 CBD/COP/17/INF/13.\n4 CBD/COP/17/INF/16.","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n發行：限閱\n2026年10月28日\n原文：英文","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1<br />\n發行：限閱<br />\n2026年10月28日<br />\n原文：英文</p>"},{"md":"生物多樣性公約\n締約方大會\n第十七次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日\n議程項目 22\n報告之採納","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約<br />\n締約方大會<br />\n第十七次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日<br />\n議程項目 22<br />\n報告之採納</p>"},{"md":"擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書\n締約方會議的\n生物多樣性公約\n締約方大會\n第十二次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日\n議程項目 19\n報告之採納","html":"<p>擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書<br />\n締約方會議的<br />\n生物多樣性公約<br />\n締約方大會<br />\n第十二次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日<br />\n議程項目 19<br />\n報告之採納</p>"},{"md":"擔任取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生之利益公平與公正分享\n名古屋議定書\n締約方會議的\n生物多樣性公約\n締約方大會\n第六次會議\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日\n議程項目 17\n報告之採納","html":"<p>擔任取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生之利益公平與公正分享<br />\n名古屋議定書<br />\n締約方會議的<br />\n生物多樣性公約<br />\n締約方大會<br />\n第六次會議<br />\n葉里溫，2026年10月19–30日<br />\n議程項目 17<br />\n報告之採納</p>"},{"md":"第一工作小組報告草案\n引言\n1.\n由 Gaute Hanssen（挪威）擔任主席的第一工作小組，已召開會議以審議生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 8 至 15、19 及 20（見第一節）、擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第十二次會議議程項目 12（見第二節），以及擔任取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生之利益公平與公正分享名古屋議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第六次會議議程項目 5 及 7 至 15（見第三節）。\n2.","html":"<p>第一工作小組報告草案<br />\n引言<br />\n1.<br />\n由 Gaute Hanssen（挪威）擔任主席的第一工作小組，已召開會議以審議生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 8 至 15、19 及 20（見第一節）、擔任卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第十二次會議議程項目 12（見第二節），以及擔任取得遺傳資源及其利用所產生之利益公平與公正分享名古屋議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第六次會議議程項目 5 及 7 至 15（見第三節）。<br />\n2.</p>"},{"md":"I.","html":"<p>I.</p>"},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>"},{"md":"生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議","html":"<p>生物多樣性公約締約方大會第十七次會議</p>","pre":"三節）。\n2.\n\nI.\n\n[待完成]\n\n"},{"md":"項目 8\n資源動員與財務機制\n(a)","html":"<p>項目 8<br />\n資源動員與財務機制<br />\n(a)</p>"},{"md":"資源動員\n3.\n第一工作小組於10月19日的第一個會議開始審議議程子項目 8 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案¹及一份秘書處關於資源動員與財務機制的說明書²。此外，亦有四份與子項目 8 (a) 相關的資訊文件發布：一份關於生物多樣性與氣候金融關係的研究³、一份關於債務永續性與公約實施關係的研究⁴，以及一份關於如何...","html":"<p>資源動員<br />\n3.<br />\n第一工作小組於10月19日的第一個會議開始審議議程子項目 8 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案¹及一份秘書處關於資源動員與財務機制的說明書²。此外，亦有四份與子項目 8 (a) 相關的資訊文件發布：一份關於生物多樣性與氣候金融關係的研究³、一份關於債務永續性與公約實施關係的研究⁴，以及一份關於如何...</p>"},{"md":"---\n¹ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 8 (a)。\n² CBD/COP/17/5。\n³ CBD/COP/17/INF/13。\n⁴ CBD/COP/17/INF/16。","html":"<hr />\n<p>¹ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 8 (a)。<br />\n² CBD/COP/17/5。<br />\n³ CBD/COP/17/INF/13。<br />\n⁴ CBD/COP/17/INF/16。</p>"}]},{"p":"p002","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p002.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n       guidance on safeguards in biodiversity finance mechanisms adopted in decisions XII/3 and 14/15\n       had been implemented, identifying good practices and lessons learned, as well as opportunities for\n       improving implementation of the guidance,5 and a non-exhaustive list of areas of convergence and\n       divergence on opportunities for broadening the contributor base. 6 A report on the workshop on\n       resource mobilization,7 held in February 2026, had also been made available as a reference document.\n       4.     Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Imen Meliane (Tunisia)\n       and Carolina Caceres (Canada), with the mandate to further discuss the draft decision, focusing on\n       options for broadening the contributor base; the annex on the additional criteria for the institutional\n       structure to operate the financial mechanism; the paragraphs on the three studies arising from the\n       sixth meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation and the amendments to those paragraphs\n       proposed by the Secretariat; and the remaining brackets in the body of the draft decision.\n       5.     [to be completed]\n\n(b)    Financial mechanism\n       6.     Working Group I began its consideration of agenda sub-item 8 (b) at its 1st session. It had\n       before it a draft decision8 and the report of the Council of the Global Environment Facility (GEF) for\n       the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention.9\n       7.     A representative of GEF made a brief presentation on the report of the GEF Council.\n       8.    Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Inka Gnittke (Germany)\n       and Wang Ye (China), with the mandate to address the outstanding issues from the sixth and seventh\n       meetings of the Subsidiary Body on Implementation, as well as additional issues arising out of in-\n       sessional negotiations under other agenda items for the present meetings, basing its work on text\n       prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat and in consultation with the contact group\n       Co-Chairs.\n       9.    At its 5th session, on 28 October, Working Group I heard a report by one of the Co-Chairs of\n       the contact group on the outcome of the group’s work.\n       10. The Chair established a group of friends of the Chair, facilitated by Ms. Gnittke and Ms. Wang\n       Ye, to foster further discussion and explore possible areas of convergence.\n       11.    [to be completed]\n\nItem 9\nPlanning, monitoring, reporting and review\n\n(a) Global review of collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal\nGlobal Biodiversity Framework\n       12. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda sub-item 9 (a) at its 1st session. It had\n       before it a draft decision.10 Five information documents had also been issued in relation to sub-\n       item 9 (a): a note on the Kunming dialogue on collective progress in the implementation of the\n       Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework in support of the global review,11 a subregional\n       synthesis of selected Parties from Eastern European States on collective progress in the\n       implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, 12 a global report on\n\n5 CBD/COP/17/INF/17.\n6 CBD/COP/17/INF/25.\n7 CBD/RM/WS/2026/1/2.\n8 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 8 (b).\n9 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.\n10 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 9 (a).\n11 CBD/COP/17/INF/21.\n12 CBD/COP/17/INF/4.\n\n\n\n2/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"於決議 XII/3 與 14/15 中採納之生物多樣性財務機制保障措施指引\n已實施，並識別良好實務與經驗教訓，以及改進指引實施之機會，^5 以及關於擴大捐助者基礎機會之趨同與分歧領域之非詳盡清單。^6 一份關於 2026 年 2 月舉行之資源動員工作坊^7 的報告，亦已作為參考文件提供。","html":"<p>於決議 XII/3 與 14/15 中採納之生物多樣性財務機制保障措施指引<br />\n已實施，並識別良好實務與經驗教訓，以及改進指引實施之機會，^5 以及關於擴大捐助者基礎機會之趨同與分歧領域之非詳盡清單。^6 一份關於 2026 年 2 月舉行之資源動員工作坊^7 的報告，亦已作為參考文件提供。</p>"},{"md":"4.\n第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Imen Meliane（突尼西亞）與 Carolina Caceres（加拿大）共同主持，其任務為進一步討論決議草案，重點關注：擴大捐助者基礎之選項；關於運作財務機制之機構結構附加標準之附件；源自執行附屬機構第六次會議之三項研究之段落，以及秘書處所提議對該等段落之修正；以及決議草案正文內剩餘之方括號文字。","html":"<p>4.<br />\n第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Imen Meliane（突尼西亞）與 Carolina Caceres（加拿大）共同主持，其任務為進一步討論決議草案，重點關注：擴大捐助者基礎之選項；關於運作財務機制之機構結構附加標準之附件；源自執行附屬機構第六次會議之三項研究之段落，以及秘書處所提議對該等段落之修正；以及決議草案正文內剩餘之方括號文字。</p>"},{"md":"5.\n[待完成]","html":"<p>5.<br />\n[待完成]</p>"},{"md":"財務機制","html":"<p>財務機制</p>","pre":"餘之方括號文字。\n\n5.\n[待完成]\n\n"},{"md":"6.\n第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 8 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案^8 以及全球環境基金（GEF）理事會針對締約方大會第十七次會議所提交之報告.^9","html":"<p>6.<br />\n第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 8 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案^8 以及全球環境基金（GEF）理事會針對締約方大會第十七次會議所提交之報告.^9</p>"},{"md":"7.\nGEF 代表就 GEF 理事會報告進行了簡短簡報。","html":"<p>7.<br />\nGEF 代表就 GEF 理事會報告進行了簡短簡報。</p>"},{"md":"8.\n第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Inka Gnittke（德國）與 Wang Ye（中國）共同主持，其任務為處理執行附屬機構第六次與第七次會議之未決事項，以及本次會議下其他議程項目之會中談判所產生之附加議題，並在其工作基礎上，使用由主席在秘書處協助下並諮詢聯絡小組共同主席後所準備之文本。","html":"<p>8.<br />\n第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Inka Gnittke（德國）與 Wang Ye（中國）共同主持，其任務為處理執行附屬機構第六次與第七次會議之未決事項，以及本次會議下其他議程項目之會中談判所產生之附加議題，並在其工作基礎上，使用由主席在秘書處協助下並諮詢聯絡小組共同主席後所準備之文本。</p>"},{"md":"9.\n於其第五屆會議（10 月 28 日），第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。","html":"<p>9.<br />\n於其第五屆會議（10 月 28 日），第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告。</p>"},{"md":"10.\n主席成立了一個主席之友小組，由 Gnittke 女士與 Wang Ye 女士協助，以促進進一步討論並探索可能的趨同領域。","html":"<p>10.<br />\n主席成立了一個主席之友小組，由 Gnittke 女士與 Wang Ye 女士協助，以促進進一步討論並探索可能的趨同領域。</p>"},{"md":"11.\n[待完成]","html":"<p>11.<br />\n[待完成]</p>"},{"md":"項目 9\n規劃、監測、報告與審查","html":"<p>項目 9<br />\n規劃、監測、報告與審查</p>"},{"md":"(a) 全球審查實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之集體進展","html":"<p>(a) 全球審查實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之集體進展</p>"},{"md":"12.\n第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 9 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案.^10 關於子項目 9 (a) 亦已發布五份資訊文件：一份關於支持全球審查之昆明對話——關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之說明，^11 一份來自東歐國家選定締約方關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之次區域綜合報告，^12 以及一份關於","html":"<p>12.<br />\n第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 9 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案.^10 關於子項目 9 (a) 亦已發布五份資訊文件：一份關於支持全球審查之昆明對話——關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之說明，^11 一份來自東歐國家選定締約方關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之次區域綜合報告，^12 以及一份關於</p>"},{"md":"---\n5 CBD/COP/17/INF/17.\n6 CBD/COP/17/INF/25.\n7 CBD/RM/WS/2026/1/2.\n8 CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 8 (b).\n9 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.\n10 CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 9 (a).\n11 CBD/COP/17/INF/21.\n12 CBD/COP/17/INF/4.","html":"<hr />\n<p>5 CBD/COP/17/INF/17.<br />\n6 CBD/COP/17/INF/25.<br />\n7 CBD/RM/WS/2026/1/2.<br />\n8 CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 8 (b).<br />\n9 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.<br />\n10 CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 9 (a).<br />\n11 CBD/COP/17/INF/21.<br />\n12 CBD/COP/17/INF/4.</p>"}]},{"p":"p003","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p003.md","en":"                                       CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n       collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity\n       Framework, 13 a voluntary peer review of the revision and implementation of the Plan national\n       concernant la protection de la nature: 3e plan à l’horizon 2030 of Luxembourg14 and a Caribbean\n       regional report on collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global\n       Biodiversity Framework.15 A summary by the Co-Chairs of the Kunming dialogue on collective\n       progress in the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework16 and the\n       report of the Kunming dialogue on collective progress in the implementation of the Kunming-\n       Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework in support of the global review 17 had also been made\n       available as reference documents.\n       13.     A statement was made by a representative of Saudi Arabia.18\n       14. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Sanne Kruid (Kingdom of\n       the Netherlands) and Sivendra Michael (Fiji), with the mandate to address the bracketed text in the\n       draft decision.\n       15. At its 5th session, Working Group I heard reports by the Co-Chairs of the contact group on the\n       outcome of the group’s work.\n       16. The Chair informed Working Group I that the draft decision would be further considered in\n       the plenary session, rather than by Working Group I.\n\n(b)    Monitoring framework for the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework\n       17. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda sub-item 9 (b) at its 1st session. It had\n       before it a draft decision.19 An information document containing a study on the alignment of the State\n       of Nature metrics with the monitoring framework of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity\n       Framework20 had also been issued in relation to the sub-item.\n       18. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Philip Raymond (United\n       Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland) and Ntakadzeni Tshidada (South Africa), with the\n       mandate to continue work on the draft decision, basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with\n       the assistance of the Secretariat.\n       19.     [to be completed]\n\nItem 10\nImplementation of Article 8(j) and other provisions of the Convention on Biological\nDiversity related to indigenous peoples and local communities\n       20.     Working Group I began its consideration of agenda sub-item 10 at its 1st session.\n       21. At the suggestion of the Chair, Working Group I agreed to consider agenda sub-items 10 (a)\n       and 10 (b) (i) together.\n\n(a) Modus operandi of the Subsidiary Body on Article 8(j) and Other Provisions of the\nConvention on Biological Diversity Related to Indigenous Peoples and Local Communities\n\n(b) (i)    Implementation of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions\nof the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 2030: guidelines\n13 CBD/COP/17/INF/7.\n14 CBD/COP/17/INF/12.\n15 CBD/COP/17/INF/22.\n16 CBD/IMP/OM/2026/1/8.\n17 CBD/IMP/OM/2026/1/9.\n18 Available here, at 37 minutes and 21 seconds into the recording.\n19 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 9 (b).\n20 CBD/COP/17/INF/3.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                        3/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"在實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要方面的集體進展$^{13}$、盧森堡關於自然保護計畫之修訂與實施自願性同儕審查：Plan national concernant la protection de la nature: 3e plan à l’horizon 2030$^{14}$，以及一份關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展的加勒比區域報告$^{15}$。此外，亦提供以下文件作為參考文件：關於昆明對話在實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展方面的共同主席摘要$^{16}$，以及旨在支持全球審查的昆明對話關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之報告$^{17}$。","html":"<p>在實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要方面的集體進展<sup>13</sup>、盧森堡關於自然保護計畫之修訂與實施自願性同儕審查：Plan national concernant la protection de la nature: 3e plan à l’horizon 2030<sup>14</sup>，以及一份關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展的加勒比區域報告<sup>15</sup>。此外，亦提供以下文件作為參考文件：關於昆明對話在實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展方面的共同主席摘要<sup>16</sup>，以及旨在支持全球審查的昆明對話關於實施昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要集體進展之報告<sup>17</sup>。</p>"},{"md":"13. 沙烏地阿拉伯代表發表了聲明$^{18}$。","html":"<p>13. 沙烏地阿拉伯代表發表了聲明<sup>18</sup>。</p>"},{"md":"14. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Sanne Kruid（荷蘭王國）與 Sivendra Michael（斐濟）共同主持，其任務為處理決議草案中的方括號文字。","html":"<p>14. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Sanne Kruid（荷蘭王國）與 Sivendra Michael（斐濟）共同主持，其任務為處理決議草案中的方括號文字。</p>"},{"md":"15. 在第五屆會議期間，第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組共同主席關於該小組工作成果的報告。","html":"<p>15. 在第五屆會議期間，第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組共同主席關於該小組工作成果的報告。</p>"},{"md":"16. 主席通知第一工作小組，決議草案將在全體會議而非第一工作小組進行進一步審議。","html":"<p>16. 主席通知第一工作小組，決議草案將在全體會議而非第一工作小組進行進一步審議。</p>"},{"md":"(b) 昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之監測架構","html":"<p>(b) 昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要之監測架構</p>"},{"md":"17. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 9 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案$^{19}$。與該子項目相關亦發布了一份資訊文件，內容包含一項關於「自然狀態指標」與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構一致性之研究$^{20}$。","html":"<p>17. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 9 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案<sup>19</sup>。與該子項目相關亦發布了一份資訊文件，內容包含一項關於「自然狀態指標」與昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要監測架構一致性之研究<sup>20</sup>。</p>"},{"md":"18. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Philip Raymond（英國）與 Ntakadzeni Tshidada（南非）共同主持，其任務為繼續進行決議草案的工作，並以主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字作為工作基礎。","html":"<p>18. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Philip Raymond（英國）與 Ntakadzeni Tshidada（南非）共同主持，其任務為繼續進行決議草案的工作，並以主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字作為工作基礎。</p>"},{"md":"19. [待完成]","html":"<p>19. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"項目 10\n關於原住民族與地方社區之《生物多樣性公約》第 8(j) 條及其他條款之實施","html":"<p>項目 10<br />\n關於原住民族與地方社區之《生物多樣性公約》第 8(j) 條及其他條款之實施</p>"},{"md":"20. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 10。","html":"<p>20. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 10。</p>"},{"md":"21. 應主席建議，第一工作小組同意共同審議議程子項目 10 (a) 與 10 (b) (i)。","html":"<p>21. 應主席建議，第一工作小組同意共同審議議程子項目 10 (a) 與 10 (b) (i)。</p>"},{"md":"(a) 關於原住民族與地方社區之《生物多樣性公約》第 8(j) 條及其他條款之附屬機構之運作方式","html":"<p>(a) 關於原住民族與地方社區之《生物多樣性公約》第 8(j) 條及其他條款之附屬機構之運作方式</p>"},{"md":"(b) (i) 關於 2030 年前實施原住民族與地方社區相關之《生物多樣性公約》第 8(j) 條及其他條款工作計畫之指南","html":"<p>(b) (i) 關於 2030 年前實施原住民族與地方社區相關之《生物多樣性公約》第 8(j) 條及其他條款工作計畫之指南</p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{13}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/7.\n$^{14}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/12.\n$^{15}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/22.\n$^{16}$ CBD/IMP/OM/2026/1/8.\n$^{17}$ CBD/IMP/OM/2026/1/9.\n$^{18}$ 可於此處，錄音 37 分 21 秒處取得。\n$^{19}$ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 9 (b)。\n$^{20}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/3.","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>13</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/7.<br />\n<sup>14</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/12.<br />\n<sup>15</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/22.<br />\n<sup>16</sup> CBD/IMP/OM/2026/1/8.<br />\n<sup>17</sup> CBD/IMP/OM/2026/1/9.<br />\n<sup>18</sup> 可於此處，錄音 37 分 21 秒處取得。<br />\n<sup>19</sup> CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 9 (b)。<br />\n<sup>20</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/3.</p>"}]},{"p":"p004","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p004.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\nto strengthen the legal and policy framework for the implementation of Targets 2 and 3 of\nthe Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, including on indigenous and\ntraditional territories, to support the protection and restoration practices led by indigenous\npeoples and local communities (Task 1.1); and guidelines for the inclusion and\nconsideration of traditional lands and of resource use in spatial planning processes and\nenvironmental impact assessments (Task 1.2)\n        22. In considering sub-items 10 (a) and 10 (b) (i), Working Group I had before it two draft\n        decisions, one for each sub-item.21 In addition, a note by the Secretariat on the informal dialogue on\n        the outcomes of the first meeting of the Subsidiary Body on Article 8(j), with a focus on its modus\n        operandi, had been issued as an information document for sub-item 10 (a).22\n        23. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Sikeade Egbuwalo\n        (Nigeria) and Jennifer Tauli Corpuz (International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity), with the\n        mandate to resolve the outstanding issues within the scope of the two sub-items, basing its work on\n        text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat and the contact group Co-Chairs.\n        24.     [to be completed]\n\n(b) (ii)    Implementation of the programme of work on Article 8(j) and other provisions\nof the Convention related to indigenous peoples and local communities to 2030: process to\nreview and update the Voluntary Glossary of Key Terms and Concepts Within the Context\nof Article 8(j) and Related Provisions of the Convention (Task 5.4)\n        25. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 10 (b) (ii) at its 1st session. It had\n        before it a draft decision.23\n        26. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised\n        version of the draft decision, in consultation with the Secretariat.\n        27. At its 4th session, on 23 October, Working Group I began its consideration of a draft decision\n        submitted by the Chair.\n        28.     A statement was made by a representative of Brazil.\n        29.     Working Group I agreed to defer consideration of the draft decision until its next session.\n        30.     [to be completed]\n\n(c)     In-depth dialogue on Article 8(j) and related provisions of the Convention\n        31. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 10 (c) at its 1st session. It had before\n        it a draft decision.24\n        32. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised\n        version of the draft decision, in consultation with the Secretariat.\n        33.     [to be completed]\n\n(d)     Recommendations of the Permanent Forum on Indigenous Issues\n        34. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 10 (d) at its 1st session. It had before\n        it a draft decision.25\n\n\n21 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-items 10 (a) and 10 (b) (i).\n22 CBD/COP/17/INF/20.\n23 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 10 (b) (ii).\n24 Ibid., sub-item 10 (c).\n25 Ibid., sub-item 10 (d).\n\n\n\n4/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"以強化執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》目標 2 與目標 3 之法律與政策框架，包括關於原住民族與傳統領地之議題，以支持由原住民族與地方社區主導之保護與復育實務（任務 1.1）；以及在空間規劃程序與環境影響評估中納入並考量傳統土地與資源利用之指南（任務 1.2）","html":"<p>以強化執行《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》目標 2 與目標 3 之法律與政策框架，包括關於原住民族與傳統領地之議題，以支持由原住民族與地方社區主導之保護與復育實務（任務 1.1）；以及在空間規劃程序與環境影響評估中納入並考量傳統土地與資源利用之指南（任務 1.2）</p>"},{"md":"22. 在審議子項目 10 (a) 與 10 (b) (i) 時，第一工作小組面前有兩份決議草案，每個子項目各有一份。$^{21}$ 此外，秘書處就關於第八條 (j) 條附屬機構第一次會議成果（重點在於其運作方式）之非正式對話所發布之說明，已作為子項目 10 (a) 之資訊文件發布。$^{22}$","html":"<p>22. 在審議子項目 10 (a) 與 10 (b) (i) 時，第一工作小組面前有兩份決議草案，每個子項目各有一份。<sup>21</sup> 此外，秘書處就關於第八條 (j) 條附屬機構第一次會議成果（重點在於其運作方式）之非正式對話所發布之說明，已作為子項目 10 (a) 之資訊文件發布。<sup>22</sup></p>"},{"md":"23. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Sikeade Egbuwalo（奈及利亞）與 Jennifer Tauli Corpuz（生物多樣性國際原住民族論壇）共同主持，其任務為解決上述兩個子項目範圍內尚未解決之議題，並在其工作基礎上，使用由主席在秘書處與聯絡小組共同主席協助下所準備之文本。","html":"<p>23. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Sikeade Egbuwalo（奈及利亞）與 Jennifer Tauli Corpuz（生物多樣性國際原住民族論壇）共同主持，其任務為解決上述兩個子項目範圍內尚未解決之議題，並在其工作基礎上，使用由主席在秘書處與聯絡小組共同主席協助下所準備之文本。</p>"},{"md":"24.","html":"<p>24.</p>"},{"md":"[to be completed]","html":"<p>[to be completed]</p>","pre":"同主席協助下所準備之文本。\n\n24.\n\n"},{"md":"(b) (ii)\n第八條 (j) 條及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關規定之工作計畫執行至 2030 年：審查並更新《第八條 (j) 條及公約相關規定脈絡下關鍵術語與概念自願性詞彙表》之程序（任務 5.4）","html":"<p>(b) (ii)<br />\n第八條 (j) 條及公約中其他與原住民族與地方社區相關規定之工作計畫執行至 2030 年：審查並更新《第八條 (j) 條及公約相關規定脈絡下關鍵術語與概念自願性詞彙表》之程序（任務 5.4）</p>"},{"md":"25. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 10 (b) (ii)。其面前有一份決議草案。$^{23}$","html":"<p>25. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 10 (b) (ii)。其面前有一份決議草案。<sup>23</sup></p>"},{"md":"26. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並在諮商秘書處後準備決議草案之修訂版本。","html":"<p>26. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並在諮商秘書處後準備決議草案之修訂版本。</p>"},{"md":"27. 在 10 月 23 日的第四屆會議中，第一工作小組開始審議由主席提交之決議草案。","html":"<p>27. 在 10 月 23 日的第四屆會議中，第一工作小組開始審議由主席提交之決議草案。</p>"},{"md":"(c)","html":"<p>(c)</p>","pre":"作小組開始審議由主席提交之決議草案。\n\n"},{"md":"28. 巴西代表發表了聲明。","html":"<p>28. 巴西代表發表了聲明。</p>"},{"md":"29. 第一工作小組同意將該決議草案之審議延後至其下一屆會議。","html":"<p>29. 第一工作小組同意將該決議草案之審議延後至其下一屆會議。</p>"},{"md":"30.","html":"<p>30.</p>"},{"md":"[to be completed]","html":"<p>[to be completed]</p>","pre":"之審議延後至其下一屆會議。\n\n30.\n\n"},{"md":"關於第八條 (j) 條及公約相關規定之深入對話","html":"<p>關於第八條 (j) 條及公約相關規定之深入對話</p>"},{"md":"31. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 10 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案。$^{24}$","html":"<p>31. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 10 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案。<sup>24</sup></p>"},{"md":"32. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並在諮商秘書處後準備決議草案之修訂版本。","html":"<p>32. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並在諮商秘書處後準備決議草案之修訂版本。</p>"},{"md":"33.","html":"<p>33.</p>"},{"md":"[to be completed]","html":"<p>[to be completed]</p>","pre":"後準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n\n33.\n\n"},{"md":"(d)","html":"<p>(d)</p>","pre":"\n[to be completed]\n\n"},{"md":"原住民族問題常設論壇之建議","html":"<p>原住民族問題常設論壇之建議</p>"},{"md":"34. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 10 (d)。其面前有一份決議草案。$^{25}$","html":"<p>34. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 10 (d)。其面前有一份決議草案。<sup>25</sup></p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{21}$ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 10 (a) 與 10 (b) (i)。\n$^{22}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/20。\n$^{23}$ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 10 (b) (ii)。\n$^{24}$ 同上，子項目 10 (c)。\n$^{25}$ 同上，子項目 10 (d)。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>21</sup> CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 10 (a) 與 10 (b) (i)。<br />\n<sup>22</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/20。<br />\n<sup>23</sup> CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 10 (b) (ii)。<br />\n<sup>24</sup> 同上，子項目 10 (c)。<br />\n<sup>25</sup> 同上，子項目 10 (d)。</p>"}]},{"p":"p005","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p005.md","en":"                                      CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        35. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised\n        version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat.\n        36.      A statement was made by a representative of the Russian Federation.\n        37.      [to be completed]\n\nItem 11\nDigital sequence information on genetic resources\n        38. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 11 at its 1st session, in conjunction\n        with item 15 of the agenda for the sixth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the\n        meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol. It had before it a draft decision.26 It also had before it\n        a note by the Secretariat on digital sequence information on genetic resources, 27 and its three\n        addenda, containing the report of the Steering Committee of the Multilateral Mechanism for the Fair\n        and Equitable Sharing of Benefits from the Use of Digital Sequence Information on Genetic\n        Resources, including the Cali Fund,28 the outcomes of the work of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert\n        Group on Allocation Methodology on the Disbursement of Funds from the Cali Fund 29 and the\n        executive summary of a study on contribution rates, including implications for revenue generation\n        and economic competitiveness, and on national and international standards for the identification of\n        small, medium and large entities.30 A note by the Secretariat containing the study itself had also been\n        issued as an information document.31\n        39. One of the Co-Chairs of the Steering Committee of the Multilateral Mechanism presented the\n        report of the Committee.\n        40. One of the Co-Chairs of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on the Allocation Methodology\n        presented the report of the Expert Group.\n        41. One of the Co-Chairs of the group of friends of the Co-Chairs established by the Subsidiary\n        Body on Implementation at its seventh meeting to work on the review methodology of effectiveness\n        of the Multilateral Mechanism reported on the work done by the group during the intersessional\n        period.\n        42. As the modalities for the early submission of statements32 had been implemented for agenda\n        item 11, with statements submitted on an informal and voluntary basis pursuant to notification\n        No. 2026-072 of the Secretariat, the Chair asked the Parties and observers listed in annex I to\n        document CBD/COP/17/INF/24 and present at the session whether they objected to their statements\n        being considered as statements officially submitted for the present item. No objections were raised.\n        43. Working Group I therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered\n        as statements officially submitted under agenda item 11: Antigua and Barbuda, Australia,\n        Bangladesh, Brazil, Canada, Costa Rica, Côte d’Ivoire, European Union and its member States, Fiji\n        (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Guatemala, Indonesia, Japan, Jordan,\n        Madagascar, Maldives, Morocco, Norway, Republic of Korea, Senegal, Switzerland, United\n        Kingdom and Viet Nam.33\n\n\n\n26 Ibid., item 11.\n27 CBD/COP/17/6.\n28 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1.\n29 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2.\n30 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.3.\n31 CBD/COP/17/INF/18.\n32 CBD/COP/17/1/Rev.1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/1/Add.2/Rev.1, annex VI.\n33 Given that item 11 was considered in conjunction of item 15 of the agenda for the sixth meeting of the Conference of the\n\nParties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol, statements submitted by Parties to the Convention that were\nalso party to the Nagoya Protocol under item 11 were considered to also apply to item 15.\n\n                                                                                                                              5/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"35. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。\n36. 俄羅斯聯邦代表發表了聲明。\n37. [待完成]","html":"<p>35. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。<br />\n36. 俄羅斯聯邦代表發表了聲明。<br />\n37. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"議程第 11 項\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊\n38. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程第 11 項，此項審議係與作為名古屋議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第六屆會議議程第 15 項併行進行。該工作小組面前有一份決議草案。$^{26}$ 此外，該工作小組面前還有秘書處關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊的一份說明$^{27}$ 及其三份附件，內容包含：利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊（包括卡利基金）以實現公平、公正與利益分享之多邊機制指導委員會之報告$^{28}$、關於卡利基金資金撥付分配方法論之特設技術專家小組工作成果$^{29}$，以及一項關於貢獻率（包括對收入產生與經濟競爭力的影響）以及關於識別中小及大型實體之國家與國際標準研究之執行摘要$^{30}$。一份包含該研究本身之秘書處說明亦已作為資訊文件發布$^{31}$。\n39. 多邊機制指導委員會的一位共同主席提交了該委員會的報告。\n40. 分配方法論特設技術專家小組的一位共同主席提交了該專家小組的報告。\n41. 由執行附屬機構在其第七屆會議上設立、旨在針對多邊機制有效性審查方法論進行工作的主席之友小組的一位共同主席，報告了該小組在會期內所完成的工作。\n42. 由於議程第 11 項已實施提早提交聲明之方式$^{32}$，即根據秘書處第 2026-072 號通知，在非正式且自願的基礎上提交聲明，因此主席詢問列於附件 I（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）之締約方與觀察員，在該會議期間是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程正式提交之聲明。現場未提出異議。\n43. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為根據議程第 11 項正式提交之聲明：安地卡及巴布達、澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、瓜地馬拉、印尼、日本、約旦、馬達加斯加、馬爾地夫、摩洛哥、挪威、大韓民國、塞內加爾、瑞士、英國及越南。$^{33}$","html":"<p>議程第 11 項<br />\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊<br />\n38. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程第 11 項，此項審議係與作為名古屋議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第六屆會議議程第 15 項併行進行。該工作小組面前有一份決議草案。<sup>26</sup> 此外，該工作小組面前還有秘書處關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊的一份說明<sup>27</sup> 及其三份附件，內容包含：利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊（包括卡利基金）以實現公平、公正與利益分享之多邊機制指導委員會之報告<sup>28</sup>、關於卡利基金資金撥付分配方法論之特設技術專家小組工作成果<sup>29</sup>，以及一項關於貢獻率（包括對收入產生與經濟競爭力的影響）以及關於識別中小及大型實體之國家與國際標準研究之執行摘要<sup>30</sup>。一份包含該研究本身之秘書處說明亦已作為資訊文件發布<sup>31</sup>。<br />\n39. 多邊機制指導委員會的一位共同主席提交了該委員會的報告。<br />\n40. 分配方法論特設技術專家小組的一位共同主席提交了該專家小組的報告。<br />\n41. 由執行附屬機構在其第七屆會議上設立、旨在針對多邊機制有效性審查方法論進行工作的主席之友小組的一位共同主席，報告了該小組在會期內所完成的工作。<br />\n42. 由於議程第 11 項已實施提早提交聲明之方式<sup>32</sup>，即根據秘書處第 2026-072 號通知，在非正式且自願的基礎上提交聲明，因此主席詢問列於附件 I（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）之締約方與觀察員，在該會議期間是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程正式提交之聲明。現場未提出異議。<br />\n43. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為根據議程第 11 項正式提交之聲明：安地卡及巴布達、澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、加拿大、哥斯大黎加、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、瓜地馬拉、印尼、日本、約旦、馬達加斯加、馬爾地夫、摩洛哥、挪威、大韓民國、塞內加爾、瑞士、英國及越南。<sup>33</sup></p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{26}$ 同上，第 11 項。\n$^{27}$ CBD/COP/17/6。\n$^{28}$ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1。\n$^{29}$ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2。\n$^{30}$ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.3。\n$^{31}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/18。\n$^{32}$ CBD/COP/17/1/Rev.1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/1/Add.2/Rev.1，附件 VI。\n$^{33}$ 鑑於第 11 項係與作為名古屋議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第六屆會議議程第 15 項併行審議，因此在第 11 項下由同時為名古屋議定書締約方的公約締約方所提交之聲明，亦被視為適用於第 15 項。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>26</sup> 同上，第 11 項。<br />\n<sup>27</sup> CBD/COP/17/6。<br />\n<sup>28</sup> CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1。<br />\n<sup>29</sup> CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2。<br />\n<sup>30</sup> CBD/COP/17/6/Add.3。<br />\n<sup>31</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/18。<br />\n<sup>32</sup> CBD/COP/17/1/Rev.1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/1/Add.2/Rev.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/1/Add.2/Rev.1，附件 VI。<br />\n<sup>33</sup> 鑑於第 11 項係與作為名古屋議定書締約方會議的締約方大會第六屆會議議程第 15 項併行審議，因此在第 11 項下由同時為名古屋議定書締約方的公約締約方所提交之聲明，亦被視為適用於第 15 項。</p>"}]},{"p":"p006","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p006.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n       44. Working Group I also agreed that the statements of the following observers be considered as\n       statements officially submitted under agenda item 11: CGIAR System Organization, Division for\n       Ocean Affairs and the Law of the Sea of the United Nations, CBD Women’s Caucus, Federal\n       University of Juiz de Fora, Japan Bioindustry Association, International Chamber of Commerce,\n       International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity, Leibniz Institute DSMZ, Secretariat of the\n       International Treaty on Plant Genetic Resources for Food and Agriculture, United Nations\n       Environment Programme and World Wide Fund for Nature International.34\n       45. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties:\n       Argentina, Brazil, Colombia, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Egypt (on behalf of the African\n       States), European Union and its member States, Fiji (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing\n       States), Ghana, Malawi, Panama, Philippines, Russian Federation, South Africa (on behalf of the\n       Group of Like-minded Megadiverse Countries), United Arab Emirates and Zimbabwe.\n       46. At its 2nd session, on 20 October, Working Group I resumed its consideration of agenda\n       item 11, in conjunction with item 15 of the agenda for the sixth meeting of the Conference of the\n       Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol.\n       47. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Bahrain, Burundi,\n       Cameroon, China, Dominican Republic, Ecuador, Ethiopia, Guatemala, India, Indonesia, Kenya,\n       Malaysia, Saudi Arabia, Senegal, South Africa, Türkiye, Uganda and Viet Nam.\n       48. Statements were also made by representatives of the CBD Alliance, the International\n       Federation of Pharmaceutical Manufacturers and Associations, the International Indigenous Forum\n       on Biodiversity and the Third World Network.\n       49. Following the exchange of views, the Chair established a group of friends of the Chair,\n       facilitated by Daniel Mukubi Kikuni (Democratic Republic of the Congo) and Thomas Greiber\n       (Germany) to consider the memorandum of understanding establishing the institutional arrangements\n       for the Cali Fund for the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits from the Use of Digital Sequence\n       Information on Genetic Resources, and other operational documents as relevant, with a view to\n       preparing a consensus text. In addition, the group could address paragraphs 29 and 30 of the draft\n       decision, on the issue of the selection of the members of the Steering Committee, or other related\n       issues, as applicable, if they were considered to offer a solution to some of the points of contention.\n       The group would conduct its work in a closed session.\n       50. In addition, Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Patience\n       Gandiwa (Zimbabwe) and Helmut Gaugitsch (Austria), with the mandate to address sections I to IX\n       of the draft decision, basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the\n       Secretariat.\n       51.     [to be completed]\n\nItem 12\nMatters relating to support mechanisms for the implementation and awareness of the\nConvention on Biological Diversity and the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity\nFramework\n\n(a)    Capacity-building and development and technical and scientific cooperation\n       52. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 12 (a) at its 1st session. It had before\n       it a draft decision.35\n\n34 Given that item 11 was considered in conjunction of item 15 of the agenda for the sixth meeting of the Conference of the\n\nParties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol, statements submitted by observers under item 11 were\nconsidered to also apply to item 15.\n35 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 12 (a).\n\n\n\n6/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"44. 第一工作小組亦同意將下列觀察員之聲明視為依議程項目 11 正式提交之聲明：CGIAR 系統組織、聯合國海洋事務及海洋法司、CBD 女性黨團、Juiz de Fora 聯邦大學、日本生物產業協會、國際商會、生物多樣性國際原住民族論壇、Leibniz Institute DSMZ、糧食及農業植物遺傳資源國際公約秘書處、聯合國環境規劃署及世界自然基金會國際事務局。³⁴","html":"<p>44. 第一工作小組亦同意將下列觀察員之聲明視為依議程項目 11 正式提交之聲明：CGIAR 系統組織、聯合國海洋事務及海洋法司、CBD 女性黨團、Juiz de Fora 聯邦大學、日本生物產業協會、國際商會、生物多樣性國際原住民族論壇、Leibniz Institute DSMZ、糧食及農業植物遺傳資源國際公約秘書處、聯合國環境規劃署及世界自然基金會國際事務局。³⁴</p>"},{"md":"45. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議期間亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、哥倫比亞、剛果民主共和國、埃及（代表非洲國家）、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、迦納、馬拉威、巴拿馬、菲律賓、俄羅斯聯邦、南非（代表志同道合的生物多樣性豐富國家集團）、阿拉伯聯合大公國及辛巴威。","html":"<p>45. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議期間亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、哥倫比亞、剛果民主共和國、埃及（代表非洲國家）、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、迦納、馬拉威、巴拿馬、菲律賓、俄羅斯聯邦、南非（代表志同道合的生物多樣性豐富國家集團）、阿拉伯聯合大公國及辛巴威。</p>"},{"md":"46. 第一工作小組於 10 月 20 日召開之第二屆會議中，結合作為名古屋議定書締約方會議召開之締約方大會第六屆會議議程項目 15，恢復對議程項目 11 之審議。","html":"<p>46. 第一工作小組於 10 月 20 日召開之第二屆會議中，結合作為名古屋議定書締約方會議召開之締約方大會第六屆會議議程項目 15，恢復對議程項目 11 之審議。</p>"},{"md":"47. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴林、蒲隆地、喀麥隆、中國、多明尼加共和國、厄瓜多、衣索比亞、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、肯亞、馬來西亞、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非、土耳其、烏干達及越南。","html":"<p>47. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴林、蒲隆地、喀麥隆、中國、多明尼加共和國、厄瓜多、衣索比亞、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、肯亞、馬來西亞、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非、土耳其、烏干達及越南。</p>"},{"md":"48. CBD 聯盟、國際醫藥製造商與協會聯合會、生物多樣性國際原住民族論壇及第三世界網絡之代表亦發表了聲明。","html":"<p>48. CBD 聯盟、國際醫藥製造商與協會聯合會、生物多樣性國際原住民族論壇及第三世界網絡之代表亦發表了聲明。</p>"},{"md":"49. 在意見交換後，主席成立了一個主席之友小組，由 Daniel Mukubi Kikuni（剛果民主共和國）與 Thomas Greiber（德國）共同主持，旨在審議關於建立「利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊以公平公正分享利益之卡利基金」制度安排之諒解備忘錄，以及其他相關之作業文件，以準備一份共識文本。此外，若該小組被認為能為某些爭議點提供解決方案，則該小組亦可處理決議草案第 29 及 30 段關於指導委員會成員遴選之議題，或其他相關議題（視適用情況而定）。該小組將於閉門會議中進行其工作。","html":"<p>49. 在意見交換後，主席成立了一個主席之友小組，由 Daniel Mukubi Kikuni（剛果民主共和國）與 Thomas Greiber（德國）共同主持，旨在審議關於建立「利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊以公平公正分享利益之卡利基金」制度安排之諒解備忘錄，以及其他相關之作業文件，以準備一份共識文本。此外，若該小組被認為能為某些爭議點提供解決方案，則該小組亦可處理決議草案第 29 及 30 段關於指導委員會成員遴選之議題，或其他相關議題（視適用情況而定）。該小組將於閉門會議中進行其工作。</p>"},{"md":"50. 此外，第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patience Gandiwa（辛巴威）與 Helmut Gaugitsch（奧地利）共同主持，其任務為處理決議草案第 I 至 IX 節，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本。","html":"<p>50. 此外，第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patience Gandiwa（辛巴威）與 Helmut Gaugitsch（奧地利）共同主持，其任務為處理決議草案第 I 至 IX 節，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本。</p>"},{"md":"51.","html":"<p>51.</p>"},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>"},{"md":"項目 12\n關於支持《生物多樣性公約》及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》實施與提升意識之支持機制相關事項\n(a)","html":"<p>項目 12<br />\n關於支持《生物多樣性公約》及《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》實施與提升意識之支持機制相關事項<br />\n(a)</p>"},{"md":"能力建構與發展，以及技術與科學合作","html":"<p>能力建構與發展，以及技術與科學合作</p>"},{"md":"52. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 12 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案.³⁵","html":"<p>52. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 12 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案.³⁵</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"³⁴ 鑑於項目 11 是結合作為名古屋議定書締約方會議召開之締約方大會第六屆會議議程項目 15 進行審議，因此觀察員依項目 11 提交之聲明亦被視為適用於項目 15。\n³⁵ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 12 (a)。","html":"<p>³⁴ 鑑於項目 11 是結合作為名古屋議定書締約方會議召開之締約方大會第六屆會議議程項目 15 進行審議，因此觀察員依項目 11 提交之聲明亦被視為適用於項目 15。<br />\n³⁵ CBD/COP/17/2, 子項目 12 (a)。</p>"}]},{"p":"p007","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p007.md","en":"                                    CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        53. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Holly Kelley-Weil (United\n        Kingdom) and Martha Mphatso Kalemba (Malawi), with the mandate to discuss the entire draft\n        decision with a view to reaching consensus on all issues currently in brackets, basing its work on text\n        prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat.\n        54. Working Group I also agreed to transmit the revised draft budget for the Global Coordination\n        Entity, contained in table 2 of annex II to the draft decision, to the contact group on budgetary\n        matters.\n        55. At its 5th session, Working Group I heard a report by one of the Co-Chairs of the contact group\n        on the outcome of the group’s work, following which it considered a draft decision submitted by the\n        Chair.\n        56. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, Switzerland and\n        United Kingdom.\n        57.     [to be completed]\n\n(b)     Clearing-house mechanism and knowledge management\n        58. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 12 (b) at its 1st session. It had before\n        it a draft decision.36\n        59. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised\n        version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat.\n        60. At its 3rd session, on 22 October, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by\n        the Chair.\n        61. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Brazil, Canada,\n        Colombia, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Egypt, European Union and its member States, Fiji\n        (on behalf of the Pacific small island developing States), Gabon, India, Iran (Islamic Republic of),\n        Norway, Russian Federation and Saudi Arabia.\n        62. Working Group I approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the\n        plenary session as draft decision CBD/COP/17/L.3.\n\n(c)     Communication, education and public awareness\n        63. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 12 (c) at its 1st session. It had before\n        it a draft decision.37\n        64. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised\n        version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat.\n        65.     At its 3rd session, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair.\n        66. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Australia, Brazil,\n        Burkina Faso, Canada, Democratic Republic of the Congo, European Union and its member States,\n        Fiji, Guatemala, India, Iran (Islamic Republic of), Morocco, Russian Federation, Switzerland and\n        Viet Nam.\n        67.     A representative of Argentina raised a point of order.\n        68. A statement was also made by a representative of the Global Youth Biodiversity Network (also\n        on behalf of the CBD Women’s Caucus).\n\n\n\n36 Ibid., sub-item 12 (b).\n37 Ibid., sub-item 12 (c).\n\n\n\n                                                                                                          7/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"53. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Holly Kelley-Weil（英國）與 Martha Mphatso Kalemba（馬拉威）共同主持，其任務為討論整個決議草案，旨在就目前所有方括號中的議題達成共識，並在其工作基礎上採用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本。\n54. 第一工作小組亦同意將決議草案附件 II 表 2 中所載之全球協調實體（Global Coordination Entity）修訂後之預算草案，提交予預算事務聯絡小組。\n55. 在第五屆會議期間，第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告，隨後審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n56. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、瑞士及英國。\n57. [待完成]","html":"<p>53. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Holly Kelley-Weil（英國）與 Martha Mphatso Kalemba（馬拉威）共同主持，其任務為討論整個決議草案，旨在就目前所有方括號中的議題達成共識，並在其工作基礎上採用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本。<br />\n54. 第一工作小組亦同意將決議草案附件 II 表 2 中所載之全球協調實體（Global Coordination Entity）修訂後之預算草案，提交予預算事務聯絡小組。<br />\n55. 在第五屆會議期間，第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告，隨後審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n56. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、瑞士及英國。<br />\n57. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"(b) 資訊交換機制與知識管理","html":"<p>(b) 資訊交換機制與知識管理</p>"},{"md":"58. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 12 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案。³⁶\n59. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商以準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n60. 在 10 月 22 日之第三屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n61. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、加拿大、哥倫比亞、剛果民主共和國、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、加彭、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、挪威、俄羅斯聯邦及沙烏地阿拉伯。\n62. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.3 提交至全體會議。","html":"<p>58. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 12 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案。³⁶<br />\n59. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商以準備決議草案之修訂版本。<br />\n60. 在 10 月 22 日之第三屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n61. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、加拿大、哥倫比亞、剛果民主共和國、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、加彭、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、挪威、俄羅斯聯邦及沙烏地阿拉伯。<br />\n62. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.3 提交至全體會議。</p>"},{"md":"(c) 溝通、教育與大眾意識","html":"<p>(c) 溝通、教育與大眾意識</p>"},{"md":"63. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 12 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案。³⁷\n64. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商以準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n65. 在第三屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n66. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、巴西、布吉納法索、加拿大、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟、瓜地馬拉、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、摩洛哥、俄羅斯聯邦、瑞士及越南。\n67. 阿根廷代表提出了一項程序性問題。\n68. 全球青年生物多樣性網絡（亦代表 CBD 女性黨團）之代表亦發表了聲明。","html":"<p>63. 第一工作小組於第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 12 (c)。其面前有一份決議草案。³⁷<br />\n64. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式諮商，並與秘書處諮商以準備決議草案之修訂版本。<br />\n65. 在第三屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n66. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、巴西、布吉納法索、加拿大、剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟、瓜地馬拉、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、摩洛哥、俄羅斯聯邦、瑞士及越南。<br />\n67. 阿根廷代表提出了一項程序性問題。<br />\n68. 全球青年生物多樣性網絡（亦代表 CBD 女性黨團）之代表亦發表了聲明。</p>"},{"md":"³⁶ 同前引，子項目 12 (b)。\n³⁷ 同前引，子項目 12 (c)。","html":"<p>³⁶ 同前引，子項目 12 (b)。<br />\n³⁷ 同前引，子項目 12 (c)。</p>"}]},{"p":"p008","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p008.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        69. Working Group I approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the\n        plenary session as draft decision CBD/COP/17/L.4.\n\nItem 13\nCooperation with international organizations and bodies established under other\nconventions\n        70. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 13 at its 1st session. It had before it\n        a draft decision38 and a progress report on cooperation with international organizations and bodies\n        established under other conventions.39 Two information documents had also been issued in relation\n        to item 13: a submission from the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations on the\n        implementation of the Target 2 Road Map 40 and a report of the United Nations Environment\n        Programme on its activities to support the implementation of the Convention on Biological Diversity\n        and its Protocols.41\n        71. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Marina von Weissenberg\n        (Finland) and Anne Nakafeero (Uganda), with a mandate to resolve the bracketed text, basing its\n        work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat.\n        72.      A statement was made by a representative of the Russian Federation.\n        73.      [to be completed]\n\nItem 14\nMainstreaming of biodiversity and engagement with subnational governments\n\n(a)     Mainstreaming of biodiversity within and across sectors\n        74. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda sub-item 14 (a) at its 1st session. It had\n        before it a draft decision.42\n        75. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Jahidul Kabir\n        (Bangladesh) and Scott Wilson (Canada), with a mandate to reach consensus on the text, basing its\n        work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat.\n        76. At its 5th session, Working Group I heard a report by one of the Co-Chairs of the contact group\n        on the outcome of the group’s work, following which it considered a draft decision submitted by the\n        Chair.\n        77.      A representative of the Secretariat provided oral corrections to the draft decision.\n        78. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Australia, Bangladesh,\n        Brazil, European Union and its member States, Gabon, Georgia, Iran (Islamic Republic of), Norway,\n        Russian Federation and United Kingdom.\n        79. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the\n        draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed by Parties.\n        80.      [to be completed]\n\n\n\n\n38 Ibid., item 13.\n39 CBD/COP/17/9.\n40 CBD/COP/17/INF/19.\n41 CBD/COP/17/INF/26.\n42 CBD/COP/17/2, sub-item 14 (a).\n\n\n\n8/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"69. 第一工作小組批准經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.4 送交全會。","html":"<p>69. 第一工作小組批准經口頭修正之決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.4 送交全會。</p>"},{"md":"議程項目 13\n與依其他公約所設立之國際組織及機構之合作\n70. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 13。其面前有一份決議草案³⁸以及一份關於與依其他公約所設立之國際組織及機構合作之進度報告³⁹。關於項目 13 亦已發布兩份資訊文件：一份由聯合國糧食及農業組織提交關於實施目標 2 路線圖⁴⁰之提案，以及一份聯合國環境規劃署關於其支持實施《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書活動之報告⁴¹。\n71. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Marina von Weissenberg（芬蘭）與 Anne Nakafeero（烏干達）共同主持，其任務為解決方括號內之文字，並在其工作基礎上採用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。\n72.\n俄羅斯聯邦代表發表了聲明。","html":"<p>議程項目 13<br />\n與依其他公約所設立之國際組織及機構之合作<br />\n70. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 13。其面前有一份決議草案³⁸以及一份關於與依其他公約所設立之國際組織及機構合作之進度報告³⁹。關於項目 13 亦已發布兩份資訊文件：一份由聯合國糧食及農業組織提交關於實施目標 2 路線圖⁴⁰之提案，以及一份聯合國環境規劃署關於其支持實施《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書活動之報告⁴¹。<br />\n71. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Marina von Weissenberg（芬蘭）與 Anne Nakafeero（烏干達）共同主持，其任務為解決方括號內之文字，並在其工作基礎上採用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。<br />\n72.<br />\n俄羅斯聯邦代表發表了聲明。</p>"},{"md":"73.\n[待完成]","html":"<p>73.<br />\n[待完成]</p>"},{"md":"議程項目 14\n生物多樣性的主流化以及與次國家級政府的參與\n(a)\n在部門內及跨部門進行生物多樣性主流化\n74. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 14 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案⁴²。\n75. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Jahidul Kabir（孟加拉）與 Scott Wilson（加拿大）共同主持，其任務為就文字達成共識，並在其工作基礎上採用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。\n76. 在其第五屆會議中，第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告，隨後審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n77.\n秘書處代表對決議草案進行了口頭修正。\n78. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、歐盟及其成員國、加彭、喬治亞、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、挪威、俄羅斯聯邦及英國。\n79. 在意見交換後，主席表示他將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n80.\n[待完成]","html":"<p>議程項目 14<br />\n生物多樣性的主流化以及與次國家級政府的參與<br />\n(a)<br />\n在部門內及跨部門進行生物多樣性主流化<br />\n74. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程子項目 14 (a)。其面前有一份決議草案⁴²。<br />\n75. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Jahidul Kabir（孟加拉）與 Scott Wilson（加拿大）共同主持，其任務為就文字達成共識，並在其工作基礎上採用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。<br />\n76. 在其第五屆會議中，第一工作小組聽取了聯絡小組其中一位共同主席關於該小組工作成果之報告，隨後審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n77.<br />\n秘書處代表對決議草案進行了口頭修正。<br />\n78. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：澳洲、孟加拉、巴西、歐盟及其成員國、加彭、喬治亞、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、挪威、俄羅斯聯邦及英國。<br />\n79. 在意見交換後，主席表示他將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。<br />\n80.<br />\n[待完成]</p>"},{"md":"____________________\n³⁸ 同上，項目 13。\n³⁹ CBD/COP/17/9。\n⁴⁰ CBD/COP/17/INF/19。\n⁴¹ CBD/COP/17/INF/26。\n⁴² CBD/COP/17/2，子項目 14 (a)。","html":"<hr />\n<p>³⁸ 同上，項目 13。<br />\n³⁹ CBD/COP/17/9。<br />\n⁴⁰ CBD/COP/17/INF/19。<br />\n⁴¹ CBD/COP/17/INF/26。<br />\n⁴² CBD/COP/17/2，子項目 14 (a)。</p>"}]},{"p":"p009","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p009.md","en":"                                    CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n(b) Engagement with subnational governments, cities and other local authorities to\nenhance the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework\n        81. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 14 (b) at its 1st session. It had before\n        it a draft decision.43 An information document on engagement with subnational governments, cities\n        and other local authorities to enhance the implementation of the Kunming-Montreal Global\n        Biodiversity Framework44 had also been issued in relation to sub-item 14 (b).\n        82. The Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision for consideration\n        at a later session.\n        83. At its 2nd session, Working Group I began its consideration of a draft decision submitted by\n        the Chair.\n        84. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, European Union and\n        its member States and Gabon.\n        85. Following the exchange of views, Working Group I agreed to defer further consideration of\n        the draft decision pending the outcome of informal discussions.\n        86.     At its 5th session, Working Group I resumed its consideration of the draft decision.\n        87. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Australia, Brazil,\n        Canada, Cuba, European Union and its member States, India, Iran (Islamic Republic of), New\n        Zealand, Russian Federation, South Africa, Tuvalu and United Kingdom.\n        88. Working Group I agreed to convene a small group of interested Parties, moderated by a\n        representative of Tuvalu, to hold informal discussions on the draft decision.\n        89.     The representative of Tuvalu reported on the outcome of the small group’s discussions.\n        90. The Chair said that informal discussions should continue and that he would prepare a revised\n        version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views\n        expressed by Parties.\n        91.     [to be completed]\n\nItem 15\nGender Plan of Action\n        92. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 15 at its 1st session. It had before it\n        a draft decision.45\n        93. The Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the draft decision for consideration\n        at a later session.\n        94.     At its 3rd session, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair.\n        95. Working Group I approved the draft decision for transmission to the plenary session as draft\n        decision CBD/COP/17/L.2.\n\nItem 19\nReview of the effectiveness of processes under the Convention on Biological Diversity and\nits Protocols\n        96. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 19 at its 1st session, in conjunction\n        with item 12 of the agenda for the twelfth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving as the\n\n43 Ibid., sub-item 14 (b).\n44 CBD/COP/17/INF/14.\n45 CBD/COP/17/2, item 15.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                          9/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"(b) 與次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局之參與，以強化《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之實施","html":"<p>(b) 與次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局之參與，以強化《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》之實施</p>"},{"md":"81. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 14 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁴³ 關於與次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局之參與，以強化《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》實施之資訊文件⁴⁴ 亦已針對子項目 14 (b) 發布。","html":"<p>81. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 14 (b)。其面前有一份決議草案。⁴³ 關於與次國家級政府、城市及其他地方當局之參與，以強化《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》實施之資訊文件⁴⁴ 亦已針對子項目 14 (b) 發布。</p>"},{"md":"82. 主席表示，他將準備一份決議草案的修訂版本，以供後續會議審議。","html":"<p>82. 主席表示，他將準備一份決議草案的修訂版本，以供後續會議審議。</p>"},{"md":"83. 在其第二屆會議中，第一工作小組開始審議由主席提交之決議草案。","html":"<p>83. 在其第二屆會議中，第一工作小組開始審議由主席提交之決議草案。</p>"},{"md":"84. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、歐盟及其成員國以及加彭。","html":"<p>84. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、歐盟及其成員國以及加彭。</p>"},{"md":"85. 在意見交換後，第一工作小組同意延後對該決議草案的進一步審議，以待非正式討論之結果。","html":"<p>85. 在意見交換後，第一工作小組同意延後對該決議草案的進一步審議，以待非正式討論之結果。</p>"},{"md":"86. 在其第五屆會議中，第一工作小組恢復對該決議草案的審議。","html":"<p>86. 在其第五屆會議中，第一工作小組恢復對該決議草案的審議。</p>"},{"md":"87. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、巴西、加拿大、古巴、歐盟及其成員國、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、紐西蘭、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、吐瓦魯及英國。","html":"<p>87. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、澳洲、巴西、加拿大、古巴、歐盟及其成員國、印度、伊朗（伊斯蘭共和國）、紐西蘭、俄羅斯聯邦、南非、吐瓦魯及英國。</p>"},{"md":"88. 第一工作小組同意召集一個由感興趣之締約方組成的小組，由吐瓦魯代表主持，就該決議草案進行非正式討論。","html":"<p>88. 第一工作小組同意召集一個由感興趣之締約方組成的小組，由吐瓦魯代表主持，就該決議草案進行非正式討論。</p>"},{"md":"89. 吐瓦魯代表報告了該小組討論之結果。","html":"<p>89. 吐瓦魯代表報告了該小組討論之結果。</p>"},{"md":"90. 主席表示，非正式討論應持續進行，且他將諮詢秘書處，並考量締約方所表達之意見，準備一份決議草案的修訂版本。","html":"<p>90. 主席表示，非正式討論應持續進行，且他將諮詢秘書處，並考量締約方所表達之意見，準備一份決議草案的修訂版本。</p>"},{"md":"91. [待完成]","html":"<p>91. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"項目 15\n性別行動計畫","html":"<p>項目 15<br />\n性別行動計畫</p>"},{"md":"92. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 15。其面前有一份決議草案。⁴⁵","html":"<p>92. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 15。其面前有一份決議草案。⁴⁵</p>"},{"md":"93. 主席表示，他將準備一份決議草案的修訂版本，以供後續會議審議。","html":"<p>93. 主席表示，他將準備一份決議草案的修訂版本，以供後續會議審議。</p>"},{"md":"94. 在其第三屆會議中，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。","html":"<p>94. 在其第三屆會議中，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。</p>"},{"md":"95. 第一工作小組通過該決議草案，並將其提交全會，作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.2。","html":"<p>95. 第一工作小組通過該決議草案，並將其提交全會，作為決議草案 CBD/COP/17/L.2。</p>"},{"md":"項目 19\n審查《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下各程序之成效","html":"<p>項目 19<br />\n審查《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下各程序之成效</p>"},{"md":"96. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 19，並與第十二次締約方大會（同時擔任各議定書締約方大會）議程之項目 12 一併進行。","html":"<p>96. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 19，並與第十二次締約方大會（同時擔任各議定書締約方大會）議程之項目 12 一併進行。</p>"},{"md":"---\n⁴³ 同上，子項目 14 (b)。\n⁴⁴ CBD/COP/17/INF/14。\n⁴⁵ CBD/COP/17/2, 項目 15。","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁴³ 同上，子項目 14 (b)。<br />\n⁴⁴ CBD/COP/17/INF/14。<br />\n⁴⁵ CBD/COP/17/2, 項目 15。</p>"}]},{"p":"p010","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p010.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol and item 14 of the agenda for the sixth meeting of\n        the Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol. It had\n        before it a draft decision for the Conference of the Parties,46 as well as a draft decision for each of\n        the Protocols. An information document containing a compilation of views from Parties on the\n        modalities for a possible Party-driven process to further improve the effectiveness of the processes\n        and meetings under the Convention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols had also been issued in\n        relation to the agenda item.47\n        97. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Patrick Luna (Brazil) and\n        Ida Hellmark (Norway), with a mandate to resolve all bracketed text in all three draft decisions,\n        basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat.\n        98.      [to be completed]\n\nItem 20\nMulti-year programme of work of the Conference of the Parties\n        99. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 20 at its 1st session. It had before it\n        a draft decision 48 and a note by the Secretariat on the multi-year programme of work of the\n        Conference of the Parties.49\n        100. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda\n        item 20, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties\n        and observers listed in annex IV to document CBD/COP/17/INF/24 and present at the session\n        whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the\n        present item. No objections were raised.\n        101. Working Group I therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered\n        as statements officially submitted under agenda item 20: Canada, Cuba, Côte d’Ivoire, Fiji (on behalf\n        of the Pacific small island developing States), Iceland, Japan, Morocco, Republic of Korea and\n        Switzerland.\n        102. Working Group I also agreed that the statements of the following observers be considered as\n        statements officially submitted under agenda item 20: Friends of the Earth International, CBD\n        Alliance and Rainforest Action Network.\n        103. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties:\n        Argentina, Brazil, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Gabon, Guatemala, India, Kenya, Peru,\n        Russian Federation, South Africa and Uganda.\n        104. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the\n        draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or\n        supported by Parties.\n        105. [to be completed]\n\n\n\n\n46 Ibid., item 19.\n47 CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2.\n48 CBD/COP/17/2, item 20.\n49 CBD/COP/17/8.\n\n\n\n10/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議，以及擔任名古屋議定書締約方會議之第六屆締約方大會議程第 14 項。其面前有一份提交予締約方大會的決議草案，⁴⁶ 以及各議定書的決議草案。一份資訊文件亦已針對該議程項目發布，其中彙編了締約方對於「為進一步提升《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下各程序與會議有效性之可能由締約方主導程序之模式」所表達之意見。⁴⁷","html":"<p>卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議，以及擔任名古屋議定書締約方會議之第六屆締約方大會議程第 14 項。其面前有一份提交予締約方大會的決議草案，⁴⁶ 以及各議定書的決議草案。一份資訊文件亦已針對該議程項目發布，其中彙編了締約方對於「為進一步提升《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下各程序與會議有效性之可能由締約方主導程序之模式」所表達之意見。⁴⁷</p>"},{"md":"97. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patrick Luna（巴西）與 Ida Hellmark（挪威）共同主持，其任務為在秘書處協助主席準備文本的基礎上，解決所有三份決議草案中的所有方括號文字。","html":"<p>97. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patrick Luna（巴西）與 Ida Hellmark（挪威）共同主持，其任務為在秘書處協助主席準備文本的基礎上，解決所有三份決議草案中的所有方括號文字。</p>"},{"md":"98.","html":"<p>98.</p>"},{"md":"[待完成]","html":"<p>[待完成]</p>","pre":"議草案中的所有方括號文字。\n\n98.\n\n"},{"md":"議程第 20 項\n締約方大會多年期工作計畫\n99. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程第 20 項。其面前有一份決議草案 ⁴⁸ 以及秘書處關於締約方大會多年期工作計畫的說明。⁴⁹","html":"<p>議程第 20 項<br />\n締約方大會多年期工作計畫<br />\n99. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程第 20 項。其面前有一份決議草案 ⁴⁸ 以及秘書處關於締約方大會多年期工作計畫的說明。⁴⁹</p>"},{"md":"100. 由於議程第 20 項已實施提早提交聲明的模式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 IV（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）所列之締約方與觀察員，在本次會議中是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。","html":"<p>100. 由於議程第 20 項已實施提早提交聲明的模式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 IV（文件編號 CBD/COP/17/INF/24）所列之締約方與觀察員，在本次會議中是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。</p>"},{"md":"101. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方的聲明視為依議程第 20 項正式提交之聲明：加拿大、古巴、象牙海岸、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、冰島、日本、摩洛哥、大韓民國及瑞士。","html":"<p>101. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方的聲明視為依議程第 20 項正式提交之聲明：加拿大、古巴、象牙海岸、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、冰島、日本、摩洛哥、大韓民國及瑞士。</p>"},{"md":"102. 第一工作小組亦同意將下列觀察員的聲明視為依議程第 20 項正式提交之聲明：地球之友國際（Friends of the Earth International）、CBD 聯盟（CBD Alliance）及雨林行動網絡（Rainforest Action Network）。","html":"<p>102. 第一工作小組亦同意將下列觀察員的聲明視為依議程第 20 項正式提交之聲明：地球之友國際（Friends of the Earth International）、CBD 聯盟（CBD Alliance）及雨林行動網絡（Rainforest Action Network）。</p>"},{"md":"103. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、剛果民主共和國、加彭、瓜地馬拉、印度、肯亞、秘魯、俄羅斯聯邦、南非及烏干達。","html":"<p>103. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、剛果民主共和國、加彭、瓜地馬拉、印度、肯亞、秘魯、俄羅斯聯邦、南非及烏干達。</p>"},{"md":"104. 在意見交換後，主席表示他將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。","html":"<p>104. 在意見交換後，主席表示他將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備一份修訂後的決議草案版本。</p>"},{"md":"105. [待完成]","html":"<p>105. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"⁴⁶ 同前引，第 19 項。\n⁴⁷ CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2。\n⁴⁸ CBD/COP/17/2，第 20 項。\n⁴⁹ CBD/COP/17/8。","html":"<p>⁴⁶ 同前引，第 19 項。<br />\n⁴⁷ CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2。<br />\n⁴⁸ CBD/COP/17/2，第 20 項。<br />\n⁴⁹ CBD/COP/17/8。</p>"},{"md":"10/17","html":"<p>10/17</p>"}]},{"p":"p011","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p011.md","en":"                               CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\nII. Twelfth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention\n    on Biological Diversity serving as the meeting of the Parties to the\n    Cartagena Protocol\nItem 12\nReview of the effectiveness of processes under\nthe Convention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols\n      106. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 12 at its 1st session, in conjunction\n      with item 19 of the agenda for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the\n      Convention and item 14 of the agenda for the sixth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving\n      as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol. It had before it a draft decision for the\n      Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol,50 as well\n      as a draft decision each for the Conference of the Parties to the Convention and the Conference of\n      the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol. An information document\n      containing a compilation of views from Parties on the modalities for a possible Party-driven process\n      to further improve the effectiveness of the processes and meetings under the Convention on\n      Biological Diversity and its Protocols had also been issued in relation to the agenda item.51\n      107. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Patrick Luna (Brazil) and\n      Ida Hellmark (Norway), with a mandate to resolve all bracketed text in all three draft decisions,\n      basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat.\n      108. [to be completed]\n\nIII. Sixth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention on\n     Biological Diversity serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya\n     Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable\n     Sharing of Benefits Arising from Their Utilization\nItem 5\nReport of the Compliance Committee\n      109. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 5 at its 2nd session. It had before it a\n      draft decision52 and the report of the Compliance Committee under the Nagoya Protocol on the work\n      of its fifth meeting.53\n      110. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda\n      item 5, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties\n      and observers listed in annex I to document CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 and present at the session\n      whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the\n      present item. No objections were raised.\n      111. Working Group I therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered\n      as statements officially submitted under agenda item 5: Brazil, Cameroon, Chad, Côte d’Ivoire,\n      European Union and its member States, Japan, Morocco, Norway, Republic of Korea and United\n      Kingdom.\n\n\n\n\n50 CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, item 12.\n51 CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7.-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2.\n52 CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, item 5.\n53 CBD/NP/MOP/6/3.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                     11/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"II. 生物多樣性公約締約方大會暨卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議第十二次會議\n議程第 12 項\n審視生物多樣性公約及其議定書下程序之成效","html":"<p>II. 生物多樣性公約締約方大會暨卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議第十二次會議<br />\n議程第 12 項<br />\n審視生物多樣性公約及其議定書下程序之成效</p>"},{"md":"106. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程第 12 項，並與締約方大會第十七次會議議程第 19 項，以及作為名古屋議定書締約方會議之第六次締約方大會議程第 14 項併行審議。該工作小組面前有一份供卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之決議草案<sup>50</sup>，以及分別供締約方大會與作為名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會之決議草案。此外，針對該議程項目，亦已發布一份資訊文件，其中彙編了締約方對於可能透過締約方主導之程序，以進一步提升生物多樣性公約及其議定書下程序與會議成效之方式所提出的意見<sup>51</sup>。","html":"<p>106. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程第 12 項，並與締約方大會第十七次會議議程第 19 項，以及作為名古屋議定書締約方會議之第六次締約方大會議程第 14 項併行審議。該工作小組面前有一份供卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之決議草案<sup>50</sup>，以及分別供締約方大會與作為名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會之決議草案。此外，針對該議程項目，亦已發布一份資訊文件，其中彙編了締約方對於可能透過締約方主導之程序，以進一步提升生物多樣性公約及其議定書下程序與會議成效之方式所提出的意見<sup>51</sup>。</p>"},{"md":"107. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patrick Luna（巴西）與 Ida Hellmark（挪威）共同主持，其任務為解決所有三份決議草案中的所有方括號文字，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。","html":"<p>107. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patrick Luna（巴西）與 Ida Hellmark（挪威）共同主持，其任務為解決所有三份決議草案中的所有方括號文字，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文字。</p>"},{"md":"108. [待完成]","html":"<p>108. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"III. 生物多樣性公約締約方大會暨關於取得遺傳資源及公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書締約方會議第六次會議\n議程第 5 項\n合規委員會報告","html":"<p>III. 生物多樣性公約締約方大會暨關於取得遺傳資源及公平公正分享利用其後所產生利益之名古屋議定書締約方會議第六次會議<br />\n議程第 5 項<br />\n合規委員會報告</p>"},{"md":"109. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程第 5 項。其面前有一份決議草案<sup>52</sup>，以及名古屋議定書合規委員會第五次會議工作報告<sup>53</sup>。","html":"<p>109. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程第 5 項。其面前有一份決議草案<sup>52</sup>，以及名古屋議定書合規委員會第五次會議工作報告<sup>53</sup>。</p>"},{"md":"110. 由於議程第 5 項已實施提早提交聲明的方式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 I（文件編號 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4）所列之締約方與觀察員，在本次會議中是否反對將其聲明視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。現場未提出異議。","html":"<p>110. 由於議程第 5 項已實施提早提交聲明的方式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，主席詢問附件 I（文件編號 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4）所列之締約方與觀察員，在本次會議中是否反對將其聲明視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。現場未提出異議。</p>"},{"md":"111. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 5 項正式提交之聲明：巴西、喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、摩洛哥、挪威、大韓民國與英國。","html":"<p>111. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程第 5 項正式提交之聲明：巴西、喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、摩洛哥、挪威、大韓民國與英國。</p>"},{"md":"---\n<sup>50</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 12。\n<sup>51</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7.-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2。\n<sup>52</sup> CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 5。\n<sup>53</sup> CBD/NP/MOP/6/3。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>50</sup> CBD/CP/MOP/12/2, 項目 12。<br />\n<sup>51</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7.-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2。<br />\n<sup>52</sup> CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 5。<br />\n<sup>53</sup> CBD/NP/MOP/6/3。</p>"},{"md":"11/17","html":"<p>11/17</p>"}]},{"p":"p012","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p012.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        112. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties:\n        Bahrain, Bangladesh, Democratic Republic of the Congo, India, Panama and South Africa (on behalf\n        of the African States).\n        113. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the\n        draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or\n        supported by Parties.\n        114. At its 3rd session, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair.\n        115. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Cameroon, Egypt,\n        Equatorial Guinea, European Union and its member States, Peru, Saudi Arabia, Seychelles and South\n        Africa.\n        116. Working Group I approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the\n        plenary session as draft decision CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.2.\n\nItem 7\nMonitoring and reporting\n        117. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 7 at its 2nd session. It had before it a\n        draft decision54 and a note by the Secretariat on monitoring and reporting.55\n        118. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda\n        item 7, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties\n        and observers listed in annex II to document CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 and present at the session\n        whether they had any objections to their statements being considered as statements officially\n        submitted for the present item. No objections were raised.\n        119. Working Group I therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered\n        as statements officially submitted under agenda item 7: Brazil, Cameroon, Chad, Côte d’Ivoire,\n        European Union and its member States, Japan, Morocco, Norway and United Kingdom.\n        120. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties:\n        Argentina, Bahrain, Bangladesh, China, Cuba, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Egypt (on behalf\n        of the African States), India, Senegal, South Africa and United Republic of Tanzania.\n        121. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the\n        draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or\n        supported by Parties.\n        122. At its 4th session, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair.\n        123. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Brazil, India and South\n        Africa.\n        124. Working Group I approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the\n        plenary session as draft decision CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.3.\n\nItem 8\nAssessment and review of the effectiveness of the Nagoya Protocol\n        125. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 8 at its 2nd session. It had before it a\n        draft decision56. A note by the Secretariat on the second assessment and review of the effectiveness\n\n\n\n54 CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, item 7.\n55 CBD/NP/MOP/6/6.\n\n56 CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, item 8.\n\n\n\n12/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"112. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：\n巴林、孟加拉、剛果民主共和國、印度、巴拿馬及南非（代表非洲國家）。\n113. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持的意見，準備決議草案的修訂版本。\n114. 第一工作小組於其第三屆會議審議了由主席提交的決議草案。\n115. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：喀麥隆、埃及、赤道幾內亞、歐盟及其成員國、秘魯、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞席爾及南非。\n116. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.2 提交至全體會議。","html":"<p>112. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：<br />\n巴林、孟加拉、剛果民主共和國、印度、巴拿馬及南非（代表非洲國家）。<br />\n113. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持的意見，準備決議草案的修訂版本。<br />\n114. 第一工作小組於其第三屆會議審議了由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n115. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：喀麥隆、埃及、赤道幾內亞、歐盟及其成員國、秘魯、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞席爾及南非。<br />\n116. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.2 提交至全體會議。</p>"},{"md":"議程項目 7\n監測與報告\n117. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 7。其面前有一份決議草案⁵⁴以及秘書處關於監測與報告的說明事項⁵⁵。\n118. 由於議程項目 7 已實施聲明提前提交之方式，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席請求附件 II 載明於 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 中的締約方與觀察員，於會議中提出對於其聲明是否被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明是否有任何異議。無人提出異議。\n119. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方的聲明視為根據議程項目 7 正式提交之聲明：巴西、喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、摩洛哥、挪威及英國。\n120. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴林、孟加拉、中國、古巴、剛果民主共和國、埃及（代表非洲國家）、印度、塞內加爾、南非及坦尚尼亞聯合共和國。\n121. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持的意見，準備決議草案的修訂版本。\n122. 第一工作小組於其第四屆會議審議了由主席提交的決議草案。\n123. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、印度及南非。\n124. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.3 提交至全體會議。","html":"<p>議程項目 7<br />\n監測與報告<br />\n117. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 7。其面前有一份決議草案⁵⁴以及秘書處關於監測與報告的說明事項⁵⁵。<br />\n118. 由於議程項目 7 已實施聲明提前提交之方式，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席請求附件 II 載明於 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 中的締約方與觀察員，於會議中提出對於其聲明是否被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明是否有任何異議。無人提出異議。<br />\n119. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方的聲明視為根據議程項目 7 正式提交之聲明：巴西、喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、歐盟及其成員國、日本、摩洛哥、挪威及英國。<br />\n120. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴林、孟加拉、中國、古巴、剛果民主共和國、埃及（代表非洲國家）、印度、塞內加爾、南非及坦尚尼亞聯合共和國。<br />\n121. 意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持的意見，準備決議草案的修訂版本。<br />\n122. 第一工作小組於其第四屆會議審議了由主席提交的決議草案。<br />\n123. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴西、印度及南非。<br />\n124. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.3 提交至全體會議。</p>"},{"md":"議程項目 8\n名古屋議定書有效性之評估與審查\n125. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 8。其面前有一份決議草案⁵⁶。一份秘書處關於第二次評估與審查有效性的說明事項……","html":"<p>議程項目 8<br />\n名古屋議定書有效性之評估與審查<br />\n125. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 8。其面前有一份決議草案⁵⁶。一份秘書處關於第二次評估與審查有效性的說明事項……</p>"},{"md":"⁵⁴ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 7。\n⁵⁵ CBD/NP/MOP/6/6。\n⁵⁶ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 8。","html":"<p>⁵⁴ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 7。<br />\n⁵⁵ CBD/NP/MOP/6/6。<br />\n⁵⁶ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 8。</p>"}]},{"p":"p013","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p013.md","en":"                                CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n       of the Nagoya Protocol on Access to Genetic Resources and the Fair and Equitable Sharing of\n       Benefits Arising from Their Utilization had been made available as a reference document.57\n       126. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised\n       version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat.\n       127. At its 4th session, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair.\n       128. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Côte d’Ivoire,\n       Djibouti, Egypt, European Union, Guatemala, India, Japan, Malawi, Mexico, Morocco, Norway,\n       South Africa, Switzerland, Uganda, United Kingdom and Zimbabwe.\n       129. The Chair invited representatives of Malawi and any other interested Parties to hold informal\n       consultations on the margins of the meeting.\n       130. A representative of Malawi subsequently reported on the outcome of the consultations.\n       131. Working Group I approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the\n       plenary session as draft decision CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.4.\n\nItem 9\nEnhancing the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol\n       132. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 9 at its 2nd session.\n       133. At the suggestion of the Chair, Working Group I agreed to consider sub-items 9 (a) to (c)\n       together.\n\n(a)    Capacity-building and development and awareness-raising\n\n(b)    Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing-House and information-sharing\n\n(c)    The Protocol in the context of the\n       Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework\n       134. In considering sub-items 9 (a) to (c), Working Group I had before it a draft decision58 and a\n       note by the Secretariat on enhancing the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol.59 An information\n       document containing updated information on benefits received from access and benefit-sharing60 had\n       also been issued in relation to agenda item 9. In addition, the report of the Informal Advisory\n       Committee to the Access and Benefit-sharing Clearing House on its sixth meeting61 and the report of\n       the Informal Advisory Committee on Capacity-building for the implementation of the Nagoya\n       Protocol on its sixth meeting62 had been made available as reference documents.\n       135. The Chair said that he would conduct informal consultations as needed and prepare a revised\n       version of the draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat.\n       136. At its 4th session, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair.\n       137. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Argentina, Egypt, European\n       Union and its member States, Guatemala, India, Japan, Mexico, Saudi Arabia, South Africa, Tuvalu,\n       Uganda, United Kingdom and Zimbabwe.\n\n\n\n57 CBD/SBI/7/7.\n58 CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, item 9.\n59 CBD/NP/MOP/6/7.\n60 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/3.\n61 CBD/NP/ABSCH-IAC/6/3.\n62 CBD/NP/CB-IAC/2026/1/4.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                      13/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"關於《名古屋以遺傳資源取得及利用其產生的利益公平分享議定書》之文件已作為參考文件提供。⁵⁷","html":"<p>關於《名古屋以遺傳資源取得及利用其產生的利益公平分享議定書》之文件已作為參考文件提供。⁵⁷</p>"},{"md":"126. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式磋商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。","html":"<p>126. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式磋商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。</p>"},{"md":"127. 在其第四屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。","html":"<p>127. 在其第四屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。</p>"},{"md":"128. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、象牙海岸、吉布地、埃及、歐盟、瓜地馬拉、印度、日本、馬拉威、墨西哥、摩洛哥、挪威、南非、瑞士、烏干達、英國及辛巴威。","html":"<p>128. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、象牙海岸、吉布地、埃及、歐盟、瓜地馬拉、印度、日本、馬拉威、墨西哥、摩洛哥、挪威、南非、瑞士、烏干達、英國及辛巴威。</p>"},{"md":"129. 主席邀請馬拉威代表及任何其他感興趣的締約方在會議期間進行非正式磋商。","html":"<p>129. 主席邀請馬拉威代表及任何其他感興趣的締約方在會議期間進行非正式磋商。</p>"},{"md":"130. 馬拉威代表隨後報告了磋商結果。","html":"<p>130. 馬拉威代表隨後報告了磋商結果。</p>"},{"md":"131. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.4 提交全會。","html":"<p>131. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正的決議草案，並將其作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.4 提交全會。</p>"},{"md":"議程第 9 項\n加強《名古屋議定書》的實施","html":"<p>議程第 9 項<br />\n加強《名古屋議定書》的實施</p>"},{"md":"132. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程第 9 項。","html":"<p>132. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程第 9 項。</p>"},{"md":"133. 應主席建議，第一工作小組同意共同審議子項目 9 (a) 至 (c)：","html":"<p>133. 應主席建議，第一工作小組同意共同審議子項目 9 (a) 至 (c)：</p>"},{"md":"(a) 能力建構、發展與意識提升","html":"<p>(a) 能力建構、發展與意識提升</p>"},{"md":"(b) 取得與利益分享資訊交換所及資訊分享","html":"<p>(b) 取得與利益分享資訊交換所及資訊分享</p>"},{"md":"(c) 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》架構下的議定書","html":"<p>(c) 《昆明－蒙特婁全球生物多樣性綱要》架構下的議定書</p>"},{"md":"134. 在審議子項目 9 (a) 至 (c) 時，第一工作小組面前有一份決議草案⁵⁸以及一份秘書處關於加強《名古屋議定書》實施的說明文件⁵⁹。此外，關於議程第 9 項，亦已發布一份包含取得與利益分享所獲利益之更新資訊的資訊文件⁶⁰。此外，取得與利益分享資訊交換所非正式諮詢委員會第六次會議的報告⁶¹，以及關於實施《名古屋議定書》之能力建構非正式諮詢委員會第六次會議的報告⁶²，均已作為參考文件提供。","html":"<p>134. 在審議子項目 9 (a) 至 (c) 時，第一工作小組面前有一份決議草案⁵⁸以及一份秘書處關於加強《名古屋議定書》實施的說明文件⁵⁹。此外，關於議程第 9 項，亦已發布一份包含取得與利益分享所獲利益之更新資訊的資訊文件⁶⁰。此外，取得與利益分享資訊交換所非正式諮詢委員會第六次會議的報告⁶¹，以及關於實施《名古屋議定書》之能力建構非正式諮詢委員會第六次會議的報告⁶²，均已作為參考文件提供。</p>"},{"md":"135. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式磋商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。","html":"<p>135. 主席表示，他將視需要進行非正式磋商，並與秘書處協商以準備決議草案的修訂版本。</p>"},{"md":"136. 在其第四屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。","html":"<p>136. 在其第四屆會議期間，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交的決議草案。</p>"},{"md":"137. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、印度、日本、墨西哥、沙烏地阿拉伯、南非、吐瓦魯、烏干達、英國及辛巴威。","html":"<p>137. 以下締約方代表發表了聲明：阿根廷、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、印度、日本、墨西哥、沙烏地阿拉伯、南非、吐瓦魯、烏干達、英國及辛巴威。</p>"},{"md":"***","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"⁵⁷ CBD/SBI/7/7。\n⁵⁸ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2，第 9 項。\n⁵⁹ CBD/NP/MOP/6/7。\n⁶⁰ CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/3。\n⁶¹ CBD/NP/ABSCH-IAC/6/3。\n⁶² CBD/NP/CB-IAC/2026/1/4。","html":"<p>⁵⁷ CBD/SBI/7/7。<br />\n⁵⁸ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2，第 9 項。<br />\n⁵⁹ CBD/NP/MOP/6/7。<br />\n⁶⁰ CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/3。<br />\n⁶¹ CBD/NP/ABSCH-IAC/6/3。<br />\n⁶² CBD/NP/CB-IAC/2026/1/4。</p>"},{"md":"13/17","html":"<p>13/17</p>"}]},{"p":"p014","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p014.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        138. Working Group I approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the\n        plenary session as draft decision CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.5.\n\nItem 10\nFinancial mechanism and resources\n        139. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 10 at its 2nd session. It had before it\n        a draft decision63 and a note by the Secretariat on the financial mechanism and resources.64 A note\n        by the Secretariat on resource mobilization and the financial mechanism 65 and the report of the\n        Council of the Global Environment Facility for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the\n        Parties to the Convention66 had also been made available as reference documents.\n        140. A representative of GEF gave a report on matters related to the financial mechanism for the\n        Nagoya Protocol.\n        141. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda\n        item 10, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties\n        and observers listed in annex III to document CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 and present at the session\n        whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the\n        present item. No objections were raised.\n        142. Working Group I therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered\n        as statements officially submitted under agenda item 10: Brazil, Cameroon, Chad, Côte d’Ivoire,\n        Eswatini, European Union and its member States, Guatemala, Japan, Morocco, Norway, Switzerland\n        and United Kingdom.\n        143. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties:\n        Argentina, Burundi, Egypt, Guatemala, India, Panama, Saudi Arabia, Senegal, South Africa and\n        Zimbabwe.\n        144. Following the exchange of views, the Chair said that he would prepare a revised version of the\n        draft decision in consultation with the Secretariat, taking into account the views expressed or\n        supported by Parties.\n        145. At its 4th session, Working Group I considered a draft decision submitted by the Chair.\n        146. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Bahrain, Egypt, European\n        Union and its member States, Guatemala, India, Mexico, Norway, South Africa, Switzerland,\n        Uganda and United Kingdom.\n        147. The Chair invited representatives of Switzerland and any other interested Parties to hold\n        informal consultations in the margins of the meeting.\n        148. A representative of Switzerland subsequently reported on the outcome of the consultations.\n        149. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties: Democratic Republic of the\n        Congo, European Union and its member States and Fiji (on behalf of the Pacific small island\n        developing States).67\n        150. Working Group I approved the draft decision, as orally amended, for transmission to the\n        plenary session as draft decision CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.6.\n\n\n\n\n63 CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, item 10.\n64 CBD/NP/MOP/6/8.\n65 CBD/COP/17/5.\n66 CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1.\n67 Available here, at 3 hours, 4 minutes and 9 seconds into the recording.\n\n\n\n14/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"138. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬提交全會作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.5。","html":"<p>138. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬提交全會作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.5。</p>"},{"md":"第 10 議程項目\n財務機制與資源\n139. 第一工作小組於其第二會議開始審議議程項目 10。其面前有決議草案⁶³以及秘書處關於財務機制與資源之說明文件⁶⁴。此外，亦提供秘書處關於資源動員與財務機制之說明文件⁶⁵，以及全球環境基金理事會第十七次締約方大會報告⁶⁶，作為參考文件。\n140. 全球環境基金（GEF）代表就與名古屋議定書財務機制相關事項進行了報告。\n141. 由於議程項目 10 已實施聲明提早提交之形式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，因此主席詢問附件 III 載明於 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 之締約方與觀察員，在本次會議中是否反對將其聲明視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。\n142. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 10 正式提交之聲明：巴西、喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、史瓦帝尼、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、摩洛哥、挪威、瑞士及英國。\n143. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：阿根廷、布隆迪、埃及、瓜地馬拉、印度、巴拿馬、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非及辛巴威。\n144. 在意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。\n145. 在第四會議中，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。\n146. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴林、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、印度、墨西哥、挪威、南非、瑞士、烏干達及英國。\n147. 主席邀請瑞士代表及任何其他感興趣之締約方，於會議期間進行非正式協商。\n148. 瑞士代表隨後報告了協商結果。\n149. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國，以及斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）⁶⁷。\n150. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬提交全會作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.6。","html":"<p>第 10 議程項目<br />\n財務機制與資源<br />\n139. 第一工作小組於其第二會議開始審議議程項目 10。其面前有決議草案⁶³以及秘書處關於財務機制與資源之說明文件⁶⁴。此外，亦提供秘書處關於資源動員與財務機制之說明文件⁶⁵，以及全球環境基金理事會第十七次締約方大會報告⁶⁶，作為參考文件。<br />\n140. 全球環境基金（GEF）代表就與名古屋議定書財務機制相關事項進行了報告。<br />\n141. 由於議程項目 10 已實施聲明提早提交之形式，且聲明係根據第 2026-072 號通知提交，因此主席詢問附件 III 載明於 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 之締約方與觀察員，在本次會議中是否反對將其聲明視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。無人提出異議。<br />\n142. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為依議程項目 10 正式提交之聲明：巴西、喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、史瓦帝尼、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、日本、摩洛哥、挪威、瑞士及英國。<br />\n143. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中發表了聲明：阿根廷、布隆迪、埃及、瓜地馬拉、印度、巴拿馬、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非及辛巴威。<br />\n144. 在意見交流後，主席表示將與秘書處協商，並考慮締約方所表達或支持之意見，準備決議草案之修訂版本。<br />\n145. 在第四會議中，第一工作小組審議了由主席提交之決議草案。<br />\n146. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：巴林、埃及、歐盟及其成員國、瓜地馬拉、印度、墨西哥、挪威、南非、瑞士、烏干達及英國。<br />\n147. 主席邀請瑞士代表及任何其他感興趣之締約方，於會議期間進行非正式協商。<br />\n148. 瑞士代表隨後報告了協商結果。<br />\n149. 下列締約方代表發表了聲明：剛果民主共和國、歐盟及其成員國，以及斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）⁶⁷。<br />\n150. 第一工作小組通過了經口頭修正之決議草案，並擬提交全會作為決議草案 CBD/NP/MOP/6/L.6。</p>"},{"md":"⁶³ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2，項目 10。\n⁶⁴ CBD/NP/MOP/6/8。\n⁶⁵ CBD/COP/17/5。\n⁶⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。\n⁶⁷ 可於錄音 3 小時 4 分 9 秒處取得。","html":"<p>⁶³ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2，項目 10。<br />\n⁶⁴ CBD/NP/MOP/6/8。<br />\n⁶⁵ CBD/COP/17/5。<br />\n⁶⁶ CBD/COP/17/5/Add.1。<br />\n⁶⁷ 可於錄音 3 小時 4 分 9 秒處取得。</p>"}]},{"p":"p015","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p015.md","en":"                                CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\nItem 11\nSpecialized international access and benefit-sharing instruments\nin the context of Article 4, paragraph 4, of the Nagoya Protocol\n      151. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 11 at its 2nd session. It had before it\n      a draft decision68 and a note by the Secretariat on specialized international access and benefit-sharing\n      instruments in the context of Article 4, paragraph 4, of the Nagoya Protocol.69\n      152. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Mery Ciacci (European\n      Union) and Henry Ndengejeho (Namibia), with the mandate to consider the implications of the note\n      on specialized international access and benefit-sharing instruments and to reach consensus on the\n      bracketed text, basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat.\n      153. [to be completed]\n\nItem 12\nGlobal multilateral benefit-sharing mechanism\n      154. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 12 at its 2nd session. It had before it\n      a note by the Secretariat on the global multilateral benefit-sharing mechanism.70\n      155. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda\n      item 12, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties\n      and observers listed in annex IV to document CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 and present at the session\n      whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the\n      present item. No objections were raised.\n      156. Working Group I therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered\n      as statements officially submitted under agenda item 12: Cameroon, Chad, Côte d’Ivoire, Eswatini,\n      European Union and its member States, Japan, Jordan, Morocco, Norway, Senegal, Switzerland and\n      United Kingdom.\n      157. In addition, statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties:\n      Argentina, Brazil, China, Eswatini, Ghana, Guatemala, India, Indonesia, Malawi (on behalf of the\n      African States), Mexico, Peru, South Africa and Uganda.\n      158. Following the exchange of views, Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-\n      chaired by Kim van Seeters (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and Héctor Conde Almeida (Cuba), with\n      the mandate to develop a draft decision on the matter, taking into account the views expressed or\n      supported by Parties.\n      159. [to be completed]\n\nItem 13\nCooperation with international organizations,\nbodies established under other conventions, and initiatives\n      160. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 13 at its 2nd session. It had before it\n      a note by the Secretariat on cooperation with international organizations, bodies established under\n      other conventions, and initiatives.71\n      161. As the modalities for the early submission of statements had been implemented for agenda\n      item 13, with statements submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072, the Chair asked the Parties\n      and observers listed in annex V to document CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 and present at the session\n\n68 CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, item 11.\n69 CBD/NP/MOP/6/9.\n70 CBD/NP/MOP/6/10.\n71 CBD/NP/MOP/6/11.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                        15/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"議程項目 11\n《名古屋議定書》第 4 條第 4 項架構下之\n專門性國際取得與利益分享機制\n151. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 11。其面前有一份決議草案⁶⁸以及秘書處關於《名古屋議定書》第 4 條第 4 項架構下之專門性國際取得與利益分享機制之說明文件⁶⁹。\n152. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Mery Ciacci（歐盟）與 Henry Ndengejeho（納米比亞）共同主持，其任務為審議關於專門性國際取得與利益分享機制說明文件之影響，並在以主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本為基礎下，就方括號文字達成共識。\n153. [待完成]","html":"<p>議程項目 11<br />\n《名古屋議定書》第 4 條第 4 項架構下之<br />\n專門性國際取得與利益分享機制<br />\n151. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 11。其面前有一份決議草案⁶⁸以及秘書處關於《名古屋議定書》第 4 條第 4 項架構下之專門性國際取得與利益分享機制之說明文件⁶⁹。<br />\n152. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Mery Ciacci（歐盟）與 Henry Ndengejeho（納米比亞）共同主持，其任務為審議關於專門性國際取得與利益分享機制說明文件之影響，並在以主席在秘書處協助下所準備之文本為基礎下，就方括號文字達成共識。<br />\n153. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"議程項目 12\n全球多邊利益分享機制\n154. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 12。其面前有一份秘書處關於全球多邊利益分享機制之說明文件⁷⁰。\n155. 由於議程項目 12 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問列於附件 IV 文件 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 之締約方與觀察員，並於會議中，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出任何反對意見。\n156. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為根據議程項目 12 正式提交之聲明：喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、史瓦帝尼、歐盟及其成員國、日本、約旦、摩洛哥、挪威、塞內加爾、瑞士及英國。\n157. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、中國、史瓦帝尼、迦納、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、馬拉威（代表非洲國家）、墨西哥、秘魯、南非及烏干達。\n158. 在交換意見後，第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Kim van Seeters（荷蘭王國）與 Héctor Conde Almeida（古巴）共同主持，其任務為考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，擬定關於該事項之決議草案。\n159. [待完成]","html":"<p>議程項目 12<br />\n全球多邊利益分享機制<br />\n154. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 12。其面前有一份秘書處關於全球多邊利益分享機制之說明文件⁷⁰。<br />\n155. 由於議程項目 12 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問列於附件 IV 文件 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 之締約方與觀察員，並於會議中，是否反對其聲明被視為針對本項目正式提交之聲明。未提出任何反對意見。<br />\n156. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為根據議程項目 12 正式提交之聲明：喀麥隆、查德、象牙海岸、史瓦帝尼、歐盟及其成員國、日本、約旦、摩洛哥、挪威、塞內加爾、瑞士及英國。<br />\n157. 此外，下列締約方代表於會議中亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、中國、史瓦帝尼、迦納、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、馬拉威（代表非洲國家）、墨西哥、秘魯、南非及烏干達。<br />\n158. 在交換意見後，第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Kim van Seeters（荷蘭王國）與 Héctor Conde Almeida（古巴）共同主持，其任務為考量締約方所表達或支持之意見，擬定關於該事項之決議草案。<br />\n159. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"議程項目 13\n與國際組織、\n依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作\n160. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 13。其面前有一份秘書處關於與國際組織、依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作之說明文件⁷¹。\n161. 由於議程項目 13 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問列於附件 V 文件 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 之締約方與觀察員，並於會議中","html":"<p>議程項目 13<br />\n與國際組織、<br />\n依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作<br />\n160. 第一工作小組於其第二屆會議開始審議議程項目 13。其面前有一份秘書處關於與國際組織、依其他公約所設立之機構及倡議之合作之說明文件⁷¹。<br />\n161. 由於議程項目 13 已實施提前提交聲明的程序，且聲明係根據通知編號 2026-072 提交，主席詢問列於附件 V 文件 CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/4 之締約方與觀察員，並於會議中</p>"},{"md":"***\n⁶⁸ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 11。\n⁶⁹ CBD/NP/MOP/6/9。\n⁷⁰ CBD/NP/MOP/6/10。\n⁷¹ CBD/NP/MOP/6/11。","html":"<hr />\n<p>⁶⁸ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 11。<br />\n⁶⁹ CBD/NP/MOP/6/9。<br />\n⁷⁰ CBD/NP/MOP/6/10。<br />\n⁷¹ CBD/NP/MOP/6/11。</p>"}]},{"p":"p016","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p016.md","en":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        whether they objected to their statements being considered as statements officially submitted for the\n        present item. No objections were raised.\n        162. Working Group I therefore agreed that the statements of the following Parties be considered\n        as statements officially submitted under agenda item 13: Chad, Côte d’Ivoire, Morocco and Norway.\n        163. Working Group I also agreed that the statements of the following observers be considered as\n        statements officially submitted under agenda item 13: Division for Ocean Affairs and the Law of the\n        Sea of the United Nations and Secretariat of the International Treaty on Plant Genetic Resources for\n        Food and Agriculture.\n        164. In addition, a statement was made in session by a representative of the World Health\n        Organization.\n        165. Working Group I took note of the information presented in document CBD/NP/MOP/6/11.\n\nItem 14\nReview of the effectiveness of processes under\nthe Convention on Biological Diversity and its Protocols\n        166. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 14 at its 1st session, in conjunction\n        with item 19 of the agenda for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the\n        Convention and item 12 of the agenda for the twelfth meeting of the Conference of the Parties serving\n        as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol. It had before it a draft decision for the\n        Conference of the Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol,72 as well as a\n        draft decision for each of the Conference of the Parties to the Convention and the Conference of the\n        Parties serving as the meeting of the Parties to the Cartagena Protocol. An information document\n        containing a compilation of views from Parties on the modalities for a possible Party-driven process\n        to further improve the effectiveness of the processes and meetings under the Convention on\n        Biological Diversity and its Protocols had also been issued in relation to the agenda item.73\n        167. Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Patrick Luna (Brazil) and\n        Ida Hellmark (Norway), with a mandate to resolve all bracketed text in all three draft decisions,\n        basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the Secretariat.\n        168. [to be completed]\n\nItem 15\nDigital sequence information on genetic resources\n        169. Working Group I began its consideration of agenda item 15 at its 1st session, in conjunction\n        with item 11 of the agenda for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the\n        Convention. It had before it a draft decision.74 It also had before it a note by the Secretariat on digital\n        sequence information on genetic resources, 75 and its three addenda, containing the report of the\n        Steering Committee of the Multilateral Mechanism for the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits\n        from the Use of Digital Sequence Information on Genetic Resources, including the Cali Fund,76 the\n        outcomes of the work of the Ad Hoc Technical Expert Group on Allocation Methodology on the\n        Disbursement of Funds from the Cali Fund77 and the executive summary of a study on contribution\n        rates, including implications for revenue generation and economic competitiveness, and on national\n\n\n\n72 CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, item 14.\n73 CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2.\n74 CBD/COP/17/2, item 11.\n75 CBD/COP/17/6.\n76 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1.\n77 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2.\n\n\n\n16/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程項目正式提交之聲明。未提出任何反對意見。\n162. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為在議程項目 13 下正式提交之聲明：查德、象牙海岸、摩洛哥及挪威。\n163. 第一工作小組亦同意將下列觀察員之聲明視為在議程項目 13 下正式提交之聲明：聯合國海洋事務及海洋法司、糧食及農業植物遺傳資源國際公約秘書處。\n164. 此外，世界衛生組織代表於會議中發表了聲明。\n165. 第一工作小組注意到文件 CBD/NP/MOP/6/11 中所呈現之資訊。","html":"<p>是否反對其聲明被視為針對本議程項目正式提交之聲明。未提出任何反對意見。<br />\n162. 因此，第一工作小組同意將下列締約方之聲明視為在議程項目 13 下正式提交之聲明：查德、象牙海岸、摩洛哥及挪威。<br />\n163. 第一工作小組亦同意將下列觀察員之聲明視為在議程項目 13 下正式提交之聲明：聯合國海洋事務及海洋法司、糧食及農業植物遺傳資源國際公約秘書處。<br />\n164. 此外，世界衛生組織代表於會議中發表了聲明。<br />\n165. 第一工作小組注意到文件 CBD/NP/MOP/6/11 中所呈現之資訊。</p>"},{"md":"項目 14\n審視《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下程序之有效性\n166. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 14，並與《公約》締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 19，以及作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的第十二次締約方大會議程項目 12 同步進行。其面前有一份針對作為名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會的決議草案，$^{72}$ 以及針對《公約》締約方大會與作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會各自的決議草案。此外，亦有一份資訊文件針對該議程項目發布，內容彙編了締約方對於可能透過締約方主導程序以進一步提升《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下程序與會議有效性之模式的意見。$^{73}$\n167. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patrick Luna（巴西）與 Ida Hellmark（挪威）共同主持，其任務為在秘書處協助下，根據主席準備之文本，解決所有三份決議草案中的所有方括號文字。\n168. [待完成]","html":"<p>項目 14<br />\n審視《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下程序之有效性<br />\n166. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 14，並與《公約》締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 19，以及作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議的第十二次締約方大會議程項目 12 同步進行。其面前有一份針對作為名古屋議定書締約方會議之締約方大會的決議草案，<sup>72</sup> 以及針對《公約》締約方大會與作為卡塔赫納生物安全議定書締約方會議之締約方大會各自的決議草案。此外，亦有一份資訊文件針對該議程項目發布，內容彙編了締約方對於可能透過締約方主導程序以進一步提升《生物多樣性公約》及其議定書下程序與會議有效性之模式的意見。<sup>73</sup><br />\n167. 第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patrick Luna（巴西）與 Ida Hellmark（挪威）共同主持，其任務為在秘書處協助下，根據主席準備之文本，解決所有三份決議草案中的所有方括號文字。<br />\n168. [待完成]</p>"},{"md":"項目 15\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊\n169. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 15，並與《公約》締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 11 同步進行。其面前有一份決議草案。$^{74}$ 其面前亦有一份秘書處關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊的說明，$^{75}$ 及其三份附件，內容包含「利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊（包括卡利基金）以實現公平、公正與平等分享利益之多邊機制」指導委員會之報告，$^{76}$ 「關於卡利基金資金撥付分配方法論之特設技術專家小組」工作成果，$^{77}$ 以及一項關於貢獻率（包括對收入產生與經濟競爭力的影響）及國家……之研究執行摘要。","html":"<p>項目 15<br />\n遺傳資源數位序列資訊<br />\n169. 第一工作小組於其第一屆會議開始審議議程項目 15，並與《公約》締約方大會第十七次會議議程項目 11 同步進行。其面前有一份決議草案。<sup>74</sup> 其面前亦有一份秘書處關於遺傳資源數位序列資訊的說明，<sup>75</sup> 及其三份附件，內容包含「利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊（包括卡利基金）以實現公平、公正與平等分享利益之多邊機制」指導委員會之報告，<sup>76</sup> 「關於卡利基金資金撥付分配方法論之特設技術專家小組」工作成果，<sup>77</sup> 以及一項關於貢獻率（包括對收入產生與經濟競爭力的影響）及國家……之研究執行摘要。</p>"},{"md":"---\n$^{72}$ CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 14。\n$^{73}$ CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2。\n$^{74}$ CBD/COP/17/2, 項目 11。\n$^{75}$ CBD/COP/17/6。\n$^{76}$ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1。\n$^{77}$ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2。","html":"<hr />\n<p><sup>72</sup> CBD/NP/MOP/6/2, 項目 14。<br />\n<sup>73</sup> CBD/COP/17/INF/15-CBD/CP/MOP/12/INF/7-CBD/NP/MOP/6/INF/2。<br />\n<sup>74</sup> CBD/COP/17/2, 項目 11。<br />\n<sup>75</sup> CBD/COP/17/6。<br />\n<sup>76</sup> CBD/COP/17/6/Add.1。<br />\n<sup>77</sup> CBD/COP/17/6/Add.2。</p>"},{"md":"16/17","html":"<p>16/17</p>"}]},{"p":"p017","zh":"CBD_documents/zh/6ae38935f82f19ef123bb771/p017.md","en":"                                   CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1\n\n        and international standards for the identification of small, medium and large entities.78 A note by the\n        Secretariat containing the study itself had also been issued as an information document.79\n        170. In addition to the statements that had been submitted pursuant to notification No. 2026-072\n        under item 11 of the agenda for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties to the\n        Convention,80 statements were made in session by representatives of the following Parties to the\n        Nagoya Protocol: Argentina, Brazil, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Egypt (on behalf of the\n        African States), European Union and its member States, Fiji (on behalf of the Pacific small island\n        developing States), Ghana, Malawi, Panama, Philippines, South Africa (on behalf of the Group of\n        Like-minded Megadiverse Countries), United Arab Emirates and Zimbabwe.\n        171. At its 2nd session, Working Group I resumed its consideration of agenda item 15, in\n        conjunction with item 11 of the agenda for the seventeenth meeting of the Conference of the Parties\n        to the Convention.\n        172. Statements were made by representatives of the following Parties to the Nagoya Protocol:\n        Bahrain, Burundi, Cameroon, China, Dominican Republic, Ecuador, Ethiopia, Guatemala, India,\n        Indonesia, Kenya, Malaysia, Saudi Arabia, Senegal, South Africa, Uganda and Viet Nam.\n        173. Statements were also made by representatives of the CBD Alliance, the International\n        Federation of Pharmaceutical Manufacturers and Associations, the International Indigenous Forum\n        on Biodiversity and the Third World Network.\n        174. Following the exchange of views, the Chair established a group of friends of the Chair,\n        facilitated by Daniel Mukubi Kikuni (Democratic Republic of the Congo) and Thomas Greiber\n        (Germany) to consider the memorandum of understanding establishing the institutional arrangements\n        for the Cali Fund for the Fair and Equitable Sharing of Benefits from the Use of Digital Sequence\n        Information on Genetic Resources, and other operational documents as relevant, with a view to\n        preparing a consensus text. In addition, the group could address paragraphs 29 and 30 of the draft\n        decision, on the issue of the selection of the members of the Steering Committee, or other related\n        issues, as applicable, if they were considered to offer a solution to some of the points of contention.\n        The group would conduct its work in a closed session.\n        175. In addition, Working Group I agreed to establish a contact group, co-chaired by Patience\n        Gandiwa (Zimbabwe) and Helmut Gaugitsch (Austria), with the mandate to address sections I to IX\n        of the draft decision, basing its work on text prepared by the Chair with the assistance of the\n        Secretariat.\n        176. [to be completed].\n\n\n                                                     __________\n\n\n\n\n78 CBD/COP/17/6/Add.3.\n79 CBD/COP/17/INF/18.\n80 See para. [xx under item 11].\n\n\n\n                                                                                                         17/17","blocks":[{"md":"CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1","html":"<p>CBD/COP/17/WG.I/L.1-CBD/CP/MOP/12/WG.I/L.1-CBD/NP/MOP/6/WG.I/L.1</p>"},{"md":"以及用於識別小型、中型及大型實體的國際標準。⁷⁸ 秘書處亦已發布一份包含該研究本身的說明文件，作為資訊文件。⁷⁹","html":"<p>以及用於識別小型、中型及大型實體的國際標準。⁷⁸ 秘書處亦已發布一份包含該研究本身的說明文件，作為資訊文件。⁷⁹</p>"},{"md":"170. 除了根據第十七次締約方大會議程第 11 項通知編號 2026-072 所提交的聲明外，⁸⁰ 會議期間，下列《名古屋議定書》締約方的代表亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、剛果民主共和國、埃及（代表非洲國家）、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、迦納、馬拉威、巴拿馬、菲律賓、南非（代表具有相似立場的生物多樣性豐富國家集團）、阿拉伯聯合大公國及辛巴威。","html":"<p>170. 除了根據第十七次締約方大會議程第 11 項通知編號 2026-072 所提交的聲明外，⁸⁰ 會議期間，下列《名古屋議定書》締約方的代表亦發表了聲明：阿根廷、巴西、剛果民主共和國、埃及（代表非洲國家）、歐盟及其成員國、斐濟（代表太平洋小島嶼開發中國家）、迦納、馬拉威、巴拿馬、菲律賓、南非（代表具有相似立場的生物多樣性豐富國家集團）、阿拉伯聯合大公國及辛巴威。</p>"},{"md":"171. 第一工作小組在其第二屆會議中，結合第十七次締約方大會議程第 11 項，恢復對議程第 15 項的審議。","html":"<p>171. 第一工作小組在其第二屆會議中，結合第十七次締約方大會議程第 11 項，恢復對議程第 15 項的審議。</p>"},{"md":"172. 下列《名古屋議定書》締約方的代表發表了聲明：巴林、蒲隆地、喀麥隆、中國、多明尼加共和國、厄瓜多、衣索比亞、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、肯亞、馬來西亞、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非、烏干達及越南。","html":"<p>172. 下列《名古屋議定書》締約方的代表發表了聲明：巴林、蒲隆地、喀麥隆、中國、多明尼加共和國、厄瓜多、衣索比亞、瓜地馬拉、印度、印尼、肯亞、馬來西亞、沙烏地阿拉伯、塞內加爾、南非、烏干達及越南。</p>"},{"md":"173. CBD 聯盟（CBD Alliance）、國際醫藥製造商與協會聯合會（International Federation of Pharmaceutical Manufacturers and Associations）、國際生物多樣性原住民族論壇（International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity）及第三世界網絡（Third World Network）的代表亦發表了聲明。","html":"<p>173. CBD 聯盟（CBD Alliance）、國際醫藥製造商與協會聯合會（International Federation of Pharmaceutical Manufacturers and Associations）、國際生物多樣性原住民族論壇（International Indigenous Forum on Biodiversity）及第三世界網絡（Third World Network）的代表亦發表了聲明。</p>"},{"md":"174. 在意見交換後，主席成立了一個主席之友小組，由 Daniel Mukubi Kikuni（剛果民主共和國）與 Thomas Greiber（德國）協調，旨在審議關於建立「卡利基金（Cali Fund）以公平公正分享利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之利益」制度安排的諒解備忘錄，以及其他相關的作業文件，以準備達成共識文本。此外，若該小組認為能為某些爭議點提供解決方案，則可處理決議草案第 29 及 30 段關於指導委員會成員選任的問題或其他相關議題（視情況而定）。該小組將在閉門會議中進行其工作。","html":"<p>174. 在意見交換後，主席成立了一個主席之友小組，由 Daniel Mukubi Kikuni（剛果民主共和國）與 Thomas Greiber（德國）協調，旨在審議關於建立「卡利基金（Cali Fund）以公平公正分享利用遺傳資源數位序列資訊之利益」制度安排的諒解備忘錄，以及其他相關的作業文件，以準備達成共識文本。此外，若該小組認為能為某些爭議點提供解決方案，則可處理決議草案第 29 及 30 段關於指導委員會成員選任的問題或其他相關議題（視情況而定）。該小組將在閉門會議中進行其工作。</p>"},{"md":"175. 此外，第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patience Gandiwa（辛巴威）與 Helmut Gaugitsch（奧地利）共同主持，其任務是處理決議草案第 I 至 IX 節，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備的文本。","html":"<p>175. 此外，第一工作小組同意成立一個聯絡小組，由 Patience Gandiwa（辛巴威）與 Helmut Gaugitsch（奧地利）共同主持，其任務是處理決議草案第 I 至 IX 節，並在其工作基礎上使用由主席在秘書處協助下所準備的文本。</p>"},{"md":"176. [待完成]。","html":"<p>176. [待完成]。</p>"},{"md":"__________","html":"<hr />"},{"md":"⁷⁸ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.3.\n⁷⁹ CBD/COP/17/INF/18.\n⁸⁰ 見第 [xx] 段，於第 11 項下。","html":"<p>⁷⁸ CBD/COP/17/6/Add.3.<br />\n⁷⁹ CBD/COP/17/INF/18.<br />\n⁸⁰ 見第 [xx] 段，於第 11 項下。</p>"},{"md":"17/17","html":"<p>17/17</p>"}]}]};
